6251	4421	0	You are misunderstanding probability.\n\nHitting 6/49 IS EASIER than hitting 6/50. So hitting the second card is easier, BUT "hitting it ONLY on the second card" is not...\n\nA is the set of possibilities "Hitting a pair on the second card"; B is "Hitting a pair ONLY on the second card, meaning I must miss the first card". B is a subset of A, and smaller than A. B is calculated by 44/50 * 6/49. 44/50 is the chance of missing the first card.\n\nIf you continue my method to the 45th card, the possibility is bigger than one (means you will always hit a pair).	2015-02-11 00:23:40.87	\N	1896
