6544	5921	0	Odds of winning against a particular hand are not hard to calculate. Odds of winning a range of hands is much more difficult, but can be easily done if you're drawing for the nuts (or what would practically be the nuts), since you don't have to take into account opponent's hands at all. This is when calculations should always be done, even by amateurs. The simplest formula recommended to beginners is count the number of outs, then x2.2-2.5% to get the probability that you complete the draw in one more card, then compare with cost of calling as proportion of pot size.	2015-05-29 18:11:02.54	\N	3335
