11234	9631	1	(A) To answer the OP's actual question, 3-3-A-Q-2 defeats 3-3-A-K-4 because the Q is lower than the K. (B) There is one exception to the "just poker hands reversed" rule: In 2-to-7 draw, a wheel is not a straight, but is ranked as no pair, A-5-4-3-2 high. (C) There are actually *three* ways to rank lowball hands: 2-to-7, A-to-5 (as in California lowball, Razz, Omaha, and most other H/L games), and A-to-6 (aces are low, straights and flushes are bad--this is often called "London Lowball")	2018-02-07 19:42:17.163	\N	937
