11813	9937	0	The issue here is that the perfect GTO strategy cannot exist in poker. It's not the same as other game that can be beaten. There's no Nash equilibrium strategy for poker simply because beating the game is opponent dependent (not skill level dependent).\n\nThe reason is that most decisions in Poker are pretty much binary (except the ones that involve bet sizing). A very bad player can make the same moves as a very good play at one street and then do completely different things on another round; similarly, the same player can make different moves based on his/her mood/condition.	2018-06-23 22:53:43.867	\N	1896
11814	9937	0	What can be mathematically perfected is a BASE strategy against "the field", but never for a particular poker match. The best BASE strategy is designed to win against maximum amount of average players for maximum amount of profit. The rough best BASE strategy is pretty much known (don't play shit hand, bet instead of call if you are going to call anyways, aggressive > passivity... etc... ) This general strategy coded in perfectly to a poker AI will probably make a shit load of money on Pokerstar, but it would not be able to "be unbeatable", that's literally impossible in poker.	2018-06-23 22:56:18.6	\N	1896
