62	2	29	27d7e7fd-059c-43bf-a517-0d2f30f18315	2012-01-10 19:42:58.917	11	\N	\N	When playing **fast** games online (~ 30 seconds of decision time), the time a person takes to decide can be a tell-tale sign. Of course, general lag, and intentionally long pauses make this an inexact science, but on average, if a person takes too long to make a decision (longer than 2/3-rds of the clock), chances are they are unsure of their choice.\r\n\r\nAs mentioned by William, the other tell-take sign is the size of the bet, and that is somewhat driven by the game interface (i.e. how easy is it to bet double, for example), etc.
