193	5	78	743df25a-af75-4e03-9638-403fadae452f	2012-01-10 22:57:20.643	58	\N	edited title	How do I calculate my expected value of shoving, including Fold Equity, in heads up play? \r\n\r\nI know several factors are involved\r\n\r\n - Pot Size\r\n - My Stack\r\n - His Stack\r\n - My chance of winning if he calls\r\n - His chance of folding when I bet\r\n\r\n
197	2	81	33bd7eaf-58f7-4db8-a92e-da2b55d363ca	2012-01-10 23:13:08.23	22	\N	\N	When he calls and you win, you earn:\r\n\r\nPotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)\r\n\r\nWhen he calls and you lose, you lose:\r\n\r\nMin(YourStack, OpponentStack)\r\n\r\nSo, if he always called, your EV would be:\r\n\r\nEV = (ChanceOfWinning * (PotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack))) - ((1 - ChanceOfWinning) * (Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)))\r\n\r\nWhen he doesn't call, you win:\r\n\r\nPotSize\r\n\r\nSo we can add that into the above:\r\n\r\nEV = (ChanceOfOpponentFolding * PotSize) + (1 - ChanceOfOpponentFolding) *(ChanceOfWinning * (PotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack))) - ((1 - ChanceOfWinning) * (Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)))\r\n
198	5	81	18d90a67-aa28-4f65-a76c-8c73e8915c01	2012-01-10 23:19:43.273	58	\N	formatting 	When he calls and you win, you earn:\r\n\r\n> PotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)\r\n\r\nWhen he calls and you lose, you lose:\r\n\r\n> Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)\r\n\r\nSo, if he always called, your EV would be:\r\n\r\n> EV = (ChanceOfWinning * (PotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack))) - ((1 - ChanceOfWinning) * (Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)))\r\n\r\nWhen he doesn't call, you win:\r\n\r\n> PotSize\r\n\r\nSo we can add that into the above:\r\n\r\n> EV = (ChanceOfOpponentFolding * PotSize) + (1 - ChanceOfOpponentFolding) *(ChanceOfWinning * (PotSize + Min(YourStack, OpponentStack))) - ((1 - ChanceOfWinning) * (Min(YourStack, OpponentStack)))\r\n
