200	5	81	49ab16d1-f070-490a-bf9f-b90c29cd222d	2012-01-10 23:21:17.827	22	\N	Replaced terms with Variables to make equations more readable	This will be pretty messy if I don't define some variables, so here goes:\r\n\r\n - P$ = Current size of the pot\r\n - S$ = Minimum of your stack vs your opponent's stack\r\n - F% = Chance of your opponent folding to your shove\r\n - W% = Chance of you winning when called\r\n\r\nWhen he calls and you win, you earn:\r\n\r\n> P$ + S$\r\n\r\nWhen he calls and you lose, you lose:\r\n\r\n> S$\r\n\r\nSo, if he always called, your EV would be:\r\n\r\n> EV = (W% * (P$ + S$)) - ((1 - W%) * S$)\r\n\r\nBut he doesn't always call. When he doesn't call, you win:\r\n\r\n> P$\r\n\r\nSo we can add that into the above:\r\n\r\n> **EV = (F% * P$) + (1 - F%) * (W% * (P$ + S$)) - ((1 - W%) * S$))**
