393	2	167	56efca5d-6e5f-4b1a-b28c-72ee0e02958b	2012-01-12 02:27:00.377	17	\N	\N	To actually have a chance at making the nuts:\r\n--\r\n\r\nYou can cover all nut flushes, and you can cover quads when the board has 3 of a kind with `A2s+`.\r\n\r\nYou'll need `22+` to cover quads when the board is paired, that also covers all full houses.\r\n\r\nStraight flushes will require every suited connecter that is 2 or less apart - `52s+, 53s+, 54s+`.  That also covers all straights.\r\n\r\nAny time a straight flush, quads, a flush, or a straight is not possible, the nuts is a set, and your pocket pairs have that.\r\n\r\nTherefore, the range is:\r\n\r\n**A2s+, 22+, 54s+, 53s+, 52s+**\r\n\r\nTo always be able to represent the nuts (have a potential nut blocker):\r\n\r\nYou have to play every hand.  If the board has 4 to a straight flush, you need to have the 5th card.
