399	5	167	5176def0-c5cc-4e56-93be-80aee799436d	2012-01-12 02:42:56.473	17	\N	deleted 343 characters in body	You have to play 100% of hands.\r\n\r\nThere is always a chance of 4 to a straight flush, and the only single card that will never make the nuts in a 4 to a straight flush is a 2 - When the board is A345x, 67 of that suit will be the nuts.  Other than that, A245x, 2356x, 3467x, ... TJKAx, TJQAx, TJQKx can all be nutted with a single card.  Since that single card could come with a 2, you need to play every hand.
400	5	167	b110241f-cdf7-41e3-a188-6c0e2427fe68	2012-01-12 03:08:31.573	17	\N	added 695 characters in body	To actually have a chance at making the nuts, or to have every nut hand in your range:\r\n--\r\n\r\nYou can cover all nut flushes,quads when the board has 3 of a kind, and straight flushes when the board has 4 or 5 to a straight flush with with `A2s+`.\r\n\r\nYou'll need `22+` to cover quads when the board is paired, that also covers all full houses.\r\n\r\nStraight flushes will require every suited connecter that is 2 or less apart - `52s+, 53s+, 54s+`.  That also covers all straights.\r\n\r\nAny time a straight flush, quads, a flush, or a straight is not possible, the nuts is a set, and your pocket pairs have that.\r\n\r\nTherefore, the range is:\r\n\r\n**A2s+, 22+, 54s+, 53s+, 52s+**\r\n\r\nTo always be able to represent the nuts (have the nuts or a blocker to the nuts):\r\n--\r\nYou have to play 100% of hands.\r\n\r\nThis is based on the assumption that if you were dealt `2s3h`, and the board came out `Ah 2h 4h 5h Ts`, you would need to have played that hand to have/represent the nuts.  If having `Ah3h` in your range satisfies the question, the answer above is correct.  Otherwise, ...\r\n\r\nThere is always a chance of 4 to a straight flush, and the only single card that will never make the nuts in a 4 to a straight flush is a 2 - When the board is A345x, 67 of that suit will be the nuts.  Other than that, A245x, 2356x, 3467x, ... TJKAx, TJQAx, TJQKx can all be nutted with a single card.  Since that single card could come with a 2, you need to play every hand.\r\n
