567	5	227	4a68cdee-00ee-4fed-b458-c896630ad526	2012-01-16 13:49:29.097	88	\N	added 613 characters in body	[Implied Odds][1] are calculated in situations where the player expects to fold in the following round if the draw is missed, thereby losing no additional bets, but expects to gain additional bets when the draw is made. Since the player expects to always gain additional bets in later rounds when the draw is made, and never lose any additional bets when the draw is missed, the extra bets that the player expects to gain, excluding his own, can fairly be added to the current size of the pot. This adjusted pot value is known as the implied pot.\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pot_odds#Implied_pot_odds
