918	2	380	1153ddc3-1b7c-4767-a99d-99ea2c6cae14	2012-01-31 03:21:55.237	120	\N	\N	Most casinos and card rooms have lower attendance, lower buy-in tourneys. They are designed for the newer players. Most of these tournaments however are likely to have a percentage of regulars so you're likely to get a good mix from experienced player down to dead money.\r\n\r\nIn smaller tourneys what you're looking for is bank-roll management and learning how to deal with different types of players.\r\n\r\nAs always, the larger the buy-in the better the 'overall' calibre of player is.\r\na $5 buy-in online vs 1500 players is very different from a $40 buy-in against 80 players at a hotel on the Las Vegas Strip.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I like smaller pickup tourneys (one or two tables) for starting out. You get to practice the game first and deal with table changing effects later. 
