983	2	403	92a4f5dc-bad8-41b5-8e6f-2381fb213bf8	2012-02-03 15:36:18.357	56	\N	\N	If you are playing a 5 card game (like Hold-Em) then only the top 5 cards play. So, in this case, there are 4 on the table (6-9) and you each have a 10, for the best possible hand a 6-10 straight. \r\n\r\nIt is also possible that you have AA, and friend KK, but the board comes out 3-4-5-6-7 and you split as you both play the best hand - the board.
