1043	2	427	fe0730b1-bd31-4186-b4df-bbc3d8f5fe82	2012-02-08 20:09:05.303	266	\N	\N	Calling the raise will leave you with around 5200 left to play for the rest of the hand.  It's a safe assumption that calling here will leave you pot committed and you will have to put the rest of your chips in at some time, either with a shove on the flop or in chunks down to the river.  Also, it's also a safe to assume that 4 betting all-in will not get villain to fold pre flop.  If you knew the villain's propensity to fold on the flop, you could try your luck with the Stop and Go play where you call his 3bet with the intention to ship it in on the flop.\r\n\r\nBut like others have said, you are most likely a dog to villains 3 bet range at this point.
