1458	2	592	77b63f69-b3db-452a-8539-df2aa55bc97d	2012-04-20 10:34:24.517	\N	user403	\N	Q-7 offsuit actually has a little higher than 50% chance of winning against a random hand. The hands closest to a return of 0% (return being probability of winning subtract the probability of losing) are Q-5 offsuit and J-5 suited. Q-5 offsuit has the worst positive return, at about 0.24%. J-5 suited is the closest starting hand to 0% return, at about -0.03%. So if you are playing against a random hand, then Q-5 offsuit would be the worst hand to play that is still "above average".\r\n\r\n[This table][1] is useful if you want to see the rank order of the hands in a heads-up game.\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://wizardofodds.com/games/texas-hold-em/2-player-game/
