1516	2	616	f5ec178e-a581-44d8-b501-04287bbe02d8	2012-04-24 07:25:56.15	407	\N	\N	I know what your supposed to do. You start by tightening your range to about 35% openings. And you stop checking back your Ax hands and c bet call down cuz that means he's check raising with a polarized range. At the same time checking back gives away your hand. So assuming he will not try to bluff you off of top pair you start chcking back a portion of your air range. For instance I will c bet any pp under the middle card I will bet any suited connectors with  back door draws and c bet ones with out and if he will stab once type of guy I peel if he won't stab than I delay c bet. On 2 tone flops I s bet hands with bdfd and give up on ones with out and won't call a bet no matter what. If he is always betting in that spot because he knows that I will start to chck back my value range and bet everything else.  Hope this helps some of you.
