1548	2	627	05d34240-7366-4549-8242-08d2d266cbce	2012-05-02 17:43:15.22	17	\N	\N	That depends on what sort of confidence level you would like to have.  You can never be 100% sure.  What you can calculate is the probability that your true win rate is within a given range, based on your measured win rate, sample size, and standard deviation.\r\n\r\nTo do this, you would take several 100 hand samples, measure average win rate, and standard deviation.  From there, it is basic statistics to calculate confidence intervals, etc.  The tough part will be collecting the required data.
