1613	2	652	e11d962b-3750-4e9c-bd47-7e02157c349d	2012-05-16 13:50:21.34	22	\N	\N	There are two major players in this field: [Hold'em Manager](http://www.holdemmanager.com/affdata/YWZmaWxpYXRlaWQ9MjU0LGNhdGVnb3J5aWQ9Nw==/) and [Poker Tracker](http://www.pokertracker.com/?a_aid=Grinderschool). Both provide the type of in-depth number crunching and statistical analysis that you're looking for, and they do it way better than anything you would roll on your own. They track things that few players would even think to look at without first seeing the information available in one of these two programs.\r\n\r\nIn my experience, Hold'em Manager has a wider array of options for cash games, giving it a slight edge there. They even have some plugins that can detect strange patterns in your opponent's play and automatically issue notes about those plays. However, something about the way Hold'em Manager imports tournament results is messed up, so that gives Poker Tracker the edge for tournaments.
