1673	2	677	2c732969-2fe6-482c-8246-6f873db18d77	2012-05-30 18:23:21.397	22	\N	\N	I'm pretty much quoting my [answer to a very similar question](http://poker.stackexchange.com/a/652/22):\r\n\r\n>There are two major players in this field: [Hold'em Manager](http://www.holdemmanager.com/affdata/YWZmaWxpYXRlaWQ9MjU0LGNhdGVnb3J5aWQ9Nw==/) and [Poker Tracker](http://www.pokertracker.com/?a_aid=Grinderschool). Both provide the type of in-depth number crunching and statistical analysis/display that you're looking for. They track things that few players would even think to look at without first seeing the information available in one of these two programs.\r\n>\r\nIn my experience, Hold'em Manager has a wider array of options for cash games, giving it a slight edge there. They even have some plugins that can detect strange patterns in your opponent's play and automatically issue notes about those plays. However, something about the way Hold'em Manager imports tournament results is messed up, so that gives Poker Tracker the edge for tournaments.
