1760	2	707	e6d38206-062d-4d7d-beb2-1ad8e1f46bb5	2012-06-30 21:13:40.45	88	\N	\N	The rules are *relative* to the online software, casino, or house you're playing in. There really are no rules per se; only common practices.\r\n\r\nFor example, many online sites now offer tables with variable minimum/maximum buyins ranging from 10-40bb, 40-100bb, or 100-250bb. Casino's from my experience will allow you to buy-in for whatever the largest stack at the table is at the time you take a seat. House rules...ask the host ;D!
