2011	2	814	c42815ad-d4c4-49ce-a48a-24a10f54c2c2	2012-09-07 20:12:15.277	563	\N	\N	1) When you receive your hole cards - relax, hold your breath and catch a moment when everyone is busy looking at their cards. Then look at your cards slowly and then think about something neutral (concentrate on a thought how you don't really care what you're holding right now). \r\n\r\nIt's better to look at your cards **before** your turn to act, otherwise you'll be on the spot and people will be watching your immidiate reaction. Especially people who have position on you.\r\n\r\n2) Think about your hands. Where you keep them. If you shuffle chips like a pro - everyone will be aware of your experience at the table. If you try to shuffle and make mistakes - \r\neveryone will spot a rookie. Keep your hands calm and feel relaxed. \r\n\r\n3) Take a second before any action. (Don't reach your chips with hands shaking when you want to bet).\r\n\r\n4) Sunglasses are lame :)\r\n\r\n5) You can watch "high stakes poker" or "poker after dark" on youtube and study the players behaviour.\r\n\r\n6) but +1 for "not talking" advice. People who talk a lot - tend to play more loose ;)\r\n
