2510	2	993	d52f6cac-288d-4c11-ada2-53eaa6653a50	2012-12-24 17:37:23.05	445	\N	\N	In [PokerStove FAQ][1];\r\n\r\n> The slider interface for setting the top N% of hands orders the hands\r\n> according to their preflop all-in equity versus three random hands.\r\n> This rather arbitrary selection was picked because it balances the\r\n> value of high cards with the value of drawing cards. It is not an\r\n> absolute ordering, and depending on the specific situation you may\r\n> want to edit that range of hands when doing equity calculations.\r\n\r\nSo, what is exactly `N%` ? Is it equal to `VPIP`/`PFR` ? How can I calculate this statistic healthy?\r\n\r\n![enter image description here][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.pokerstove.com/blog/faq/\r\n  [2]: http://i.stack.imgur.com/PagJs.png
