2571	2	1014	2a94e723-00fe-4fe9-9f55-9337b192a37b	2013-01-04 01:17:54.927	355	\N	\N	I think the writer is arguing that calling with A5 is a bad idea preflop, while your italicized thoughts from the callers position are talking about post flop.  Post flop, I think A5 on a an A65 rainbow board is a strong hand; however preflop A5 is fairly weak.\r\n\r\nThe "Great" sentence from the excerpt is the writer putting the caller (who holds A5) on single paired Ace with a kicker less than a K (like A7, A8, ... AQ), which are each far more likely than A6 or A5.
