2696	2	1058	2d17e096-4118-4ea0-9c12-1630290bab0a	2013-01-23 10:43:11.343	713	\N	\N	In his book "The theory of poker" David Sklansky, states that in order to call an early open/raise you should hold at least the same or tighter range of your open/raiser opponent. Sklansky call this fact "gap concept". But as the first round of bets go ahead, players are facing with better pot odds that can lead a villian to call with a wider range of starting hands. How can we unify this two point of view?
