2933	2	1155	110d8bc4-9e8a-4bdf-bff2-df4775dd6324	2013-02-22 22:27:56.337	217	\N	\N	Figure out why your new game is different from the old one. For instance, in Hold'em, you get to see only two cards before the betting starts whereas in stud you get to see three, even though they are both seven card games. Also, hold 'em has five "community" cards, whereas in stud, all your cards are private. In draw, you see five cards before the betting round, and if you replace two, seven cards in total, but not all at once.
2915	2	1142	ff4226ab-0dc2-4985-ae99-336c126ed5fb	2013-02-20 17:22:30.32	803	\N	\N	You should make an effort to understand -why- you play the way that you play. \r\n\r\nSome strategies may be right in Zynga games that are not right in real-money games. The question to answer is WHY.\r\n\r\nBecause there are real money games that play like Zynga games.\r\nAnd Zynga games that play like WSOP final tables.\r\n\r\nThe location of the game is immaterial.\r\nThe only thing that matters are the players.\r\n\r\nUnderstanding why one strategy works in Zynga and another strategy works at the Pub is key to being a great poker player, because you'll find that you can apply those strategies in other situations.
