2987	2	1176	7b2fc2bb-c4e7-4450-ba2a-c1ae829b2fe7	2013-02-26 19:28:04.693	56	\N	\N	The best explanation I [found was][1]:\r\n\r\n> **Action Only** - An all-in wager which is not large enough to re-open the\r\n> betting for someone who has already acted is referred to as action\r\n> only (as opposed to a bet, which could be raised by someone who has\r\n> already acted).\r\n\r\nIt's a little confusing. "Your Action" clearly states it's your turn to do *something* (bet, fold, raise, etc.). In this situation, your actions have been locked by the all-in. The All-in wasn't a raise, as the amount wasn't a legal raise, so instead we say it's "action only" and your choice is limited.\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.poker-vibe.com/poker/terms/
