3009	2	1183	a02c8a7d-3228-4e16-a763-3bbed3cd07ff	2013-03-04 13:53:01.73	88	\N	\N	There may be a few instances that are relative to the setting in which they are used. The numbering, I'm confident, will always move in the direction in which game play progresses. I haven't seen, and doubt I ever will, anything other than that.\r\n\r\nSome examples...\r\n\r\n - In a casino seat one (1) is almost always be the seat directly to the left of the dealer, if there is a dealer. This is independent of the "Button".\r\n - If there isn't a dealer, the numbering will almost certainly move in the direction of the game flow, starting with one (1) for the SB, two (2) for the BB and so on for the remaining players, until the "Button".\r\n - There are other conventions that use, as you said you know, the UTG, HJ, CO, BU, SB, BB labels. UTG can carry extra information such as UTG**+1**, UTG**+2**, etc.\r\n\r\nI haven't seen or know of any others than these.\r\n\r\n
