3728	2	1470	e744aa17-75a9-43b8-92cb-51f4e7e2cf57	2013-08-01 05:27:22.147	674	\N	\N	To understand how to calculate these types of questions yourself, here is how you would do it:\r\n\r\nSince this hand could be dealt two ways (A♥ and 5♠ or 5♠ and A♥) and be the "same hand" for the purposes of poker, you would need to be dealt either of those two cards on the first hole card that you get and the other card on the second hole card that you get.  (This assumes that we are calculating the odds for being dealt a specific hand twice in a row as in your example.) \r\n\r\nTo calculate the likelihood of being dealt the hand once, the math looks like this:\r\n\r\n<code>\r\n` ` ` ` ` `    2 cards   ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  1 card  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` `2  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  1 ` ` ` ` ` `  ` `  \r\n  \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-  ` ` ×  ` ` ` ` ` ` \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-    ` ` ` `   = ` ` ` `  \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-  ` ` ` `   = ` ` ` `  \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-  \r\n  52 cards in deck  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  ` ` `  51 cards remaining in deck` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `2652  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `1326 ` ` ` `\r\n</code>\r\n\r\nThen, the odds that it will be dealt two hands in a row would be the odds of it being dealt the first time multiplied by the odds of it being dealt on the second hand (the same):\r\n\r\n<code>\r\n` `  1  ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` 1 ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `1 `  ` ` ` ` ` ` `  \r\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- ` ` ` `  ×  ` ` \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-  ` ` ` `   = ` ` ` `  \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-   \r\n` `1326 ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `1326 ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` ` `  1,758,276\r\n</code>\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso known as:  1,758,276 to 1 (which is the answer to your question).\r\n
