3766	2	1488	a4dc0f8b-89b2-4a80-9f44-9446649d8e2d	2013-08-08 10:21:49.14	1023	\N	\N	I don't think you will find any "official" rules about this situation because in most "official" poker tournaments/cash games the players do not deal themselves anyway.\r\n\r\nIt would be a bad idea to skip his deal because, as you already pointed out, this would disturb the seating positions. Just have someone deal for him - in the right order of course (clockwise, starting with the SB). Since this is a home game, you can make the rules - just make sure everyone knows and agrees to them.
