4039	2	1606	52db1cc0-09a6-45c8-bce1-ffe7907fc22c	2013-10-29 02:24:05.45	1147	\N	\N	Before I start, let me say that if you are from outside the US I would definitely take advantage of sites that offer rake-based-membership. In the US, we have [DragTheBar][1], which offers free membership based on the rake taken from your hands at Carbon Poker. \r\n\r\nI would even go a step further and say try every single site that offers a free trial. Stagger them (start a new trial as the other ends) and you'll be set for months. Just make sure to cancel before the trial expires.\r\n\r\n_Note: Because I'm a beginner, I will only offer recommendations for the beginner levels. My current game is Cash, 4-tabling 6Max 5NL. If you play Tournaments (MTT, SnG) then you'll want sites geared for those as well._\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n# Beginners\r\nGenerally, you should be playing the micros (2NL-50NL). Because of this, you'll want to focus on sites who also focus on the micros. And while there are plenty of sites that focus on _beginners_, you really want to focus on _micros_.\r\n\r\n## Training Site - [Drag the Bar][2]\r\nIf for any other reason, check Drag the Bar because [BlackRain79][3] is a coach there. He was (is?) the #1 micro stakes player [in the world][4] in terms of ridiculous volume and profit. The coaches there are great and in my narrow experience, seem to be far more prepared than on other sites.\r\n\r\n## Community - [CardsChat][5]\r\nAs a beginner you'll be slammed with too much information anyways, so it's important that the information is as easily accessible as possible (and easy to ask). [TwoPlusTwo][6] is in the top 3 thousand sites visited in the US. That's huge, but in my opinion it's too huge. Unless I land on 2p2 through Google, it's just too intimidating for the beginner [me].\r\n\r\nCardsChat is simple - all the top level forums can almost fit on a single screen! I'm only just now breaking out of my social-shell, but once I get a certain number of posts I'll also be eligible for their Freeroll tournaments...and you can too.\r\n\r\nTheir [strategy articles][7] are also well organized and will get you competently playing in an afternoon.\r\n\r\n## Runner Ups\r\n### Training Sites\r\n* [BlueFirePoker][8] - I used to use this way back in the day. Leatherass coaches there, and that guy [literally changed his brains physiology][9] from playing so much...so yea.\r\n* [Deuces Cracked][10] - Really fun videos, but the quality can be hit/miss (imo)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis doesn't answer your question (beginner to advance), but it was too long to leave as a comment so there you go :)\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.dragthebar.com/freepokertraining/\r\n  [2]: http://dragthebar.com\r\n  [3]: http://www.blackrain79.com/\r\n  [4]: http://www.blackrain79.com/p/coaching.html\r\n  [5]: http://www.cardschat.com/\r\n  [6]: http://forumserver.twoplustwo.com/\r\n  [7]: http://www.cardschat.com/poker-strategy.php\r\n  [8]: http://www.bluefirepoker.com/\r\n  [9]: http://www.cardplayer.com/poker-blogs/51-dusty-leatherass-schmidt/entries/561296-this-is-my-brain-on-poker\r\n  [10]: http://www.deucescracked.com/\r\n  [11]: http://www.audible.com/search/ref=a_mn_at_fre_tseft__galileo?advsearchKeywords=poker&x=-1074&y=-41
