5153	2	2651	60e82adf-18f8-4932-98b8-61ccbefe1458	2013-12-13 09:36:32.023	1144	\N	\N	that is good question. I was thinking about this as well. I found it useful in some scenarios. Consider this: you got very strong hand and at first you don't know if your opponent(s) are interested in playing further, so you don't bet allowing them to see free card and extract some value on further streets. But as soon as one of the opponent bets - that means there is a possibility of him having a hand and it is possible that he will pay back your raise. That is one situation I find check-raising useful. From the same reason it might be good when bluffing...\r\n\r\nFurther more you need to keep in mind that successful check-raise creates bigger pot then just a bet.
