5340	2	2724	c9a353d4-1a8e-4354-b5b3-2ad90e6a5146	2014-02-07 22:18:49.85	1150	\N	\N	It's not clear what you're asking, because it's not clear what you mean by "round" in this context. That said, the only options P1 has are to call, raise, or fold. P1 could only check if he had already matched the highest bet (which he hasn't, because of the raise). P2 then has to call the highest bet, raise it, or fold, for the same reasons.\r\n\r\nThe fact that P4 folded has no impact on what options P1 and P2 have.
5341	5	2724	085a5780-9c2b-4de1-9496-b268c1cd62b7	2014-02-07 22:35:05.643	1150	\N	added 298 characters in body	The only options P1 has are to call, raise, or fold. P1 could only check if he had already matched the highest bet (which he hasn't, because of the raise). P2 then has to call the highest bet, raise it, or fold, for the same reasons.\r\n\r\nThe fact that P4 folded has no impact on what options P1 and P2 have.\r\n\r\n**Edit based on comment:** The round (pre-flop, flop, turn, or river) only ends when (1) only one player is left or (2) all remaining players have matched the highest total bet made during the round. So, if the example you gave was the play after the flop cards were dealt, then the flop round continues until all players call the highest bet or only one player remains. Only then does the river come out.
5342	2	2725	ef53589f-2207-437c-9440-fd46313522aa	2014-02-08 11:35:23.47	1305	\N	\N	I'm wondering let's say this situation:\r\n\r\n    at the flop: (mainpot: 400)\r\n    P1. All in 100\r\n    P2. All in 50\r\n    P3. Rise 200\r\n    P4. Call 200\r\n\r\nIf I'm right, that would give us: \r\n\r\n    Mainpot: (400 + (50*4))-> p1,p2,p3,p4\r\n    Sidepot 1: (50 * 3)  -> p1,p3,p4\r\n    Sidepot 2: (100 * 2) -> p3,p4\r\n\r\nbut then both P3 and P4, have to quit the game (disconnected or something), what happens with sidepot 2?\r\n
