5409	2	2752	6db1a03c-119f-426a-88f7-1f40fff94c83	2014-02-17 17:47:12.037	1303	\N	\N	When I get busted it is because I did not identify that my opponent held a set and I thought my top pair with top kicker is best.\r\n\r\nI often run in situations where I held something like A&spades;K&spades; and flop looks like 4&hearts;A&diamond;7&clubs;.\r\n\r\nIt happens often that I see preflop someone limping and than still calling my 5-7xBB.\r\n\r\nNow it happens that someone with 4&diamond;4&clubs; plays slow or aggressive or whatever, but I never give them 77 or 44, nor 47 or AA - just because of their preflop betting. And I bet, he raises or goes allin and in most cases it ends in an Allin on the flop.\r\n\r\n**What is a good strategy to identify such set of fours?**\r\n\r\nOr is it impossible? Because there are so many bad players out there, that play such cards like they do and on long term they will loose but in this case they get me?\r\n\r\nI know, I have to look at stack sizes and how the guy played his last hands and everything. But I did not figure out a good way against such donk-moves.
