5417	2	2754	52032601-d2a9-4cb7-bafc-1d199f5060d2	2014-02-19 01:55:55.113	44	\N	\N	Don't blame the "bad players" for you losing all your money with a one-pair hand.  If limp-calling a low pair preflop vs you is making them money when they hit their set, it's not them that is playing poorly, but you.  They are playing profitably because you are paying off time after time.\r\n\r\nI'm not trying to be harsh, but to shine the light of reality on your assumptions.\r\n\r\nYour basic flaw is two-fold:\r\n\r\n1. You have a tendency to over-value TPTK hands.  They aren't worth all the money as often as you seem to think.\r\n2. You aren't listening when the opponent tells you they have a lock.  They are telling you this when they start shoveling money in the pot.\r\n\r\n\r\n
