5807	2	2907	aac67ac6-444f-4c8a-a324-78076019d399	2014-04-21 06:31:33.76	1363	\N	\N	Poker is typically played "table-stakes" which means that a player cannot bet more money/chips than is setting on the table in front of him. The only thing that would prevent infinite reraises between two determined players is that one (or both) running out of money to bet.\r\n\r\nIn heads-up play, as soon as one player goes all-in and is called (or calls all-in), the betting is over, the dealer deals the remaining cards for the hand and the players show their hands and the high hand wins. (Actually, the players' hands are typically shown as the last call is made, but I don't think this is required.)
5808	5	2907	6d64cf05-da67-437f-a270-304c5b138ed9	2014-04-21 06:37:20.913	1363	\N	deleted 5 characters in body	Poker is typically played "table-stakes" which means that a player cannot bet more money/chips than is setting on the table in front of him. The only thing that would prevent infinite reraises between two determined players is one (or both) running out of money to bet.\r\n\r\nIn heads-up play, as soon as one player goes all-in and is called (or calls all-in), the betting is over, the dealer deals the remaining cards for the hand and the players show their hands and the high hand wins. (Actually, the players' hands are typically shown as the last call is made, but I don't think this is required.)
