7055	5	4004	f55d1007-e4e5-4983-8f12-ad00f2caf359	2014-06-14 18:49:25.037	217	\N	added 162 characters in body	You were leading all the way, until the river card paired his hand (K-high vs.6-high). He was drawing to the "idiot" end of a gut shot straight.\r\n\r\nThe "donk bet" on third told you everything. He had "nothing" but wanted to bet, just to see how you react. There are two ways to play, neither of which you adopted.\r\n\r\n"Bet him in" by raising (small), then bet small on fourth street, since you are a favorite (until the last card). You'll lose this hand, but win many others at higher stakes.\r\n\r\n"Bet him out" by calling on third, then betting on fourth. You can win the hand right there without seeing the fifth card.\r\n\r\nBasically, your problem is that you didn't use your advantage while you had one, and gave him a "free roll" for the fifth card.\r\n\r\nThe idea is to maximize your win expectation, not to lose the minimum. The way to "lose the minimum" is to never bet. (Then you'd never win anything, either.)
