7299	2	4102	f9ea79e8-39f6-4ebb-b96c-2848a1b45511	2014-07-23 07:50:51.6	683	\N	\N	In the scenario you've mentioned, I'd personally be inclined to bet the pot rather than shoving as it is the best of both worlds.\r\n\r\nIf you're called or re-raised, you know they have something. Whereas if they call your shove, all your money is committed.\r\n\r\nSure if you hit a set later you can play a stop and go or such like.\r\n\r\nTo me, getting your money in good is about playing the odds. Gutshots and miracle cards happen but if you at least put your money in with the odds on your side, you played the hand with the best information you had.
