7903	5	4335	1cf43210-18df-434c-a341-e2b7e662672b	2014-11-04 22:27:29.447	1762	\N	added 888 characters in body	Kill pots are pots were a larger blind is posted by the winner of the pot. This is called killing the pot or the kill. The conditions for killing a pot vary as do the size of the kill.\r\n\r\nThe size of kills are generally "Full Kill" and "Half Kill". Half kill the blind posted by the person killing the pot is increased by half. With a full kill the blind is doubled.\r\n\r\nThe condition that forces the kill is typically pot size or a player winning two pots back to back. There is also a draw poker kill were the player can make a live raise with their first one or two cards. The live raise just like a live blind gives the player an option to raise once all other action is complete.\r\n\r\n[Kill game (poker)][1] From Wikipedia\r\n\r\nKills only apply to rotating dealer games like Hold'em, Omaha and draw poker were there are blinds.  \r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kill_game_(poker)
