7962	2	4358	5dcd8ce9-9574-418b-b13a-0cd6a130a712	2014-11-17 03:16:36.13	1478	\N	\N	The king on the river gave your opponent two pair, kings and nines. It also changed your best hand, giving you two pair, kings and nines. Your opponent had a queen kicker, which plays on this board and is the sole difference between your hand and your opponent's. In hold-em, the best hand is determined by the best 5-card combination of cards for each player at showdown.\r\n\r\nYour opponent's best 5-card hand here: K&spades;K&diamond;9&clubs;9&spades;Q&diamond;\r\n\r\nYour best 5-card hand: K&spades;K&diamond;9&clubs;9&hearts;4&spades;\r\n\r\nHad the board not paired on the river (and as long as the river is not a queen), you would have won this hand with your two pair versus your opponent's one pair of nines.
