8135	2	4425	7b049b35-3ac1-4feb-b142-4b4a71756132	2014-12-17 05:13:41.123	1762	\N	\N	The short answer is yes, always. Most poker rooms and rule books state plainly that you must table your cards face up to have any claim to a pot. Tabling your cards means placing them face up on the table, so that all players can see them. If you say my hand is the board and muck your cards your hand is dead and you will have no claim on the pot.
