8265	2	4474	a8a0127b-d586-4e13-886d-c9c71e1ce43d	2014-12-31 22:54:31.48	283	\N	\N	With that many players in the pot you should have raised rather than slow play. A raise of half to 3/4 the pot makes it mathematically a bad decision for anyone on a draw to call. But you could get a call from someone who hit the flop with less than a set. If someone on a draw makes the bad decision and calls, it makes no difference if you win or lose that pot since you are ahead. In the long run, this type of play wins more than it loses.
