9367	2	5515	0a1fb23d-d46c-44de-babb-839492f882db	2015-01-14 14:30:41.517	1478	\N	\N	BowlOfRed's answer is the strictly correct way this is done, but I've seen poker rooms where the convention is to give a new chip to any player with remaining odd lower-denomination chips.  So, if they were coloring up to eliminate the $100 chips and replacing them with $500 chips, if you had between 1 and 4 $100 chips, you'd receive 1 $500 chip to replace them.
