9428	5	5538	83e281af-ba3d-4b8c-aa5d-81f596faa17a	2015-01-21 01:13:37.247	1762	\N	Corrected sentence structure.	The game was Texas Holdem NLHE 1$/2$  6 player game. \r\nI was in the big blind. Two players limped in, one of them was a new player.. I got Q&spades;Q&hearts; and made a standard `3BB` raise. both players called.\r\n\r\nThe flop came with A&hearts;A&diamond;7&spades;. I made `50%` pot bet and was called by the new player, the other player folded.\r\n\r\nThe turn came with A&spades; so we had 3 aces on the table. I  decided to bet the pot and I was re-raised all-in. I called and the player shows down A&clubs;Q&diamond; I lost the pot.\r\n\r\nI am wondering whether I played this hand correctly?
