9476	2	5563	e661bd3b-a2ef-460f-89fb-877e1e297104	2015-01-25 16:22:50.38	3001	\N	\N	Hmmm, I think you are confused. There is no such thing as a legal 'minimum raise' - some gambling houses might insist on at least a big blind, but it is not a rule.\r\n\r\nIt actually a phrase meaning a player has made a 'minimum raise', i.e. they have raised but by possibly the smallest amount. They have not made any attempt at extravagance in betting to show off or bluff or intimidate, but just said 'okay i'm in'. Essentially a minimum raise is a 'limp', although limping refers to a player with a strong hand making a MR, which is tactics and depends on the environment and mood of the player in question.
