9503	2	5582	8583c078-9874-4e64-a43a-6448fa87a47b	2015-01-26 09:38:36.407	1856	\N	\N	From my experience at Party, you either wait until the BB comes round to you before being dealt in, or you have to put a BB dead in the pot on your first hand. Different sites may vary.\r\n\r\nThe reason is not just positional advantage; if it were not the case then you could be dealt hands for free then quit before playing a blind - with enough patience you could keep leaving and returning, folding everything other than premium pairs and getting a major advantage. Obviously there's no strict rule on leaving - if the BB is not just about to reach you then you're losing out by giving up "free" hands.
