 that marginal-pair when the flop hits, you need to protect that set by betting something you can be confident will weed out the stragglers who are chasing something on the back-end that will dominate you. \r\n\r\nYou're lucky to have won the hand (you DID win the hand, right? or am I reading that wrong?) because anyone could've hit a straight given how many folks you let come with you, and because you didn't protect your hand by increasing its perceived value, you left the outcome up to chance, and you should limit that as much as possible with smart play and skill.
