9790	2	5694	7038e05e-c930-4b1a-818b-cbedc86c0b3f	2015-02-20 21:53:40.583	1478	\N	\N	Yes.  You must use exactly two cards from your hand to make your best 5-card poker hand, so if there were three 9's on the board your best hand would use the 9 and the highest ranked other card from your hand.  For example, if you held KQ97 and the board were 999AJ, your best hand would use the 9 and K, for a best hand of 9999K. Of course, in this case the kicker is meaningless, since no other player can also have quad 9's.\r\n
