9867	2	5724	446e3d2e-0967-4f0f-be10-eb838aee0f1d	2015-03-06 19:35:26.897	1084	\N	\N	Both players have two pairs, as their is a pair of King's on the board. Inclinations was ahead until the river paired the board.\r\n\r\nRubina's best five card hand is two pair: K&hearts;K&spades;6&diamond;6&clubs;T&diamond; \r\n\r\nWhich beats Inclinations best five card hand: K&hearts;K&spades;6&hearts;6&clubs;5&diamond;\r\n\r\nThe two pairs are equal in rank, so the fifth card acts as the tie breaker.\r\n\r\nAlso check my answer here, for a more in-depth explanation of how to determine who has the best hand: http://poker.stackexchange.com/a/4405/1084
