10246	2	5848	6566a738-74d4-4e6d-9212-0af2a01bb542	2015-04-19 07:20:40.38	309	\N	\N	OK, so you have:\r\n\r\n- Board: 3&diamond; 9&spades; A&spades; 4&spades; 8&spades;\r\n- Player 1: Q&spades; 9&diamond;\r\n- Player 2: K&spades; J&diamond;\r\n- Player 3: Q&clubs; 5&spades;\r\n\r\nWell, combining the 5 best cards, each player will have:\r\n\r\n- Player 1: A flush: A&spades; Q&spades; 9&spades; 8&spades; 4&spades;\r\n- Player 2: A flush: A&spades; K&spades; 9&spades; 8&spades; 4&spades;\r\n- Player 3: High-Card: A&spades; Q&clubs; 9&spades; 8&spades; 5&spades;\r\n\r\nTherefore the winner is player 2 because his King is bigger than player 1's Queen, so his flush is better.
