10523	2	5949	45e9dca5-ea85-4f51-ab85-263086ca48aa	2015-06-06 21:19:21.237	3143	\N	\N	I've been playing a lot more tournaments recently and I'm not sure how well I've been managing my stack. Last night I found myself one of the big stacks at  the table: I had 55 on the button and the Villain with 12BBs goes all in from Hijack. Figuring he's shoving a lot of AX and maybe some smaller pairs, I make the call in the knowledge that I'm probably entering a coin flip. Villain has AJ of hearts and ends up hitting a flush. \r\n\r\nI'm probably getting the equity to call here but should I really be letting a player get into a coin flip with me in tournament play? I was the second biggest stack at the table at the time and it cost about 1/5 of my stack to make the call.\r\n\r\n
