10572	2	5970	9f2d6c5e-7a44-479a-80f8-53e679e9b6a5	2015-06-13 10:14:44.59	1846	\N	\N	I played following hand in NLHE microstakes online money game (6 seats):\r\n\r\nEvery one is in a deep stack (above **100BB**)\r\n\r\nI have A&hearts;Q&spades;\r\n\r\nBefore flop:\r\n\r\nI raised **3BB** next player reraised to **10BB** and I called. The reason I called was that I had <50% chance to win this pot if my opponent has a pair. I wanted to decide about next action when flop appears (give up when miss the flop or play when I hit the flop) \r\n\r\nFlop (**21BB**):\r\n\r\nK&hearts;J&diamond;T&hearts;\r\n\r\nQuickly saying bingo! I have the best possible hand now. The only issue is how much I can win now.\r\nI call and my opponent raises **10BB** then I call it.\r\n\r\nTurn (**41BB**):\r\n\r\n4&clubs;\r\nI call, my opponent raises **41BB**. I call him.\r\n\r\nRiver (**123BB**):\r\nJ&spades;\r\n\r\nNow if my opponent had pocket kings (more probable) or pocket tens or jacks, he wins.\r\n\r\nWe have both called.\r\n\r\nThe opponent shows A&spades;A&diamond; I won the pot.\r\n\r\nDespite I won the pot, I am not sure if I could win more here. Here are my thoughts:\r\n\r\n - On preflop I should either reraise or fold it. If my opponent is raising me, it means that he has >JJ or AK or he is bluffing.\r\n - I played correctly on flop\r\n - As I knew that I have the best hand, on turn I should reraise and then (if there is not appearing any card making him a potential full house) raise again on the river. I could win more money then\r\n\r\nAlso I am also not sure if my opponent played correctly on turn. IMO he should raise only half of the pot, not entire pot.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if my thinking is correct.
