11061	2	6165	3ac723a3-f2bb-4ebe-bbd5-ed677ca9bb87	2015-08-18 00:50:46.373	\N	user1165	\N	This pot is split since the _kickers_ never get a chance to be used.\r\n\r\nTexas Hold'em is all about making the _5-best combination of cards_, regardless of how many of your hole cards are used.\r\n\r\nIn this particular example, the players have this hand:\r\n\r\nPlayer 1 hand:  T&hearts; T&diamond; A&clubs; A&diamond; J&spades;\r\n\r\nPlayer 2 hand:  T&hearts; T&diamond; A&clubs; A&hearts; J&spades;\r\n\r\nAs you see, their hand is identical; they both have `2-pair`.\r\n\r\nTheir `kickers` are never used since there is already `a higher rank` in the board, the `J`. And since the `J` is the 5th card, the hand stops there and kickers are never used.\r\n\r\nThis is a well hidden `advantage` of ace-rags if the board gets paired.
