11189	2	6215	080f8db1-263b-436f-933c-302091ef22ec	2015-08-28 20:17:22.66	1478	\N	\N	You're looking at it from the skewed perspective where you already have four cards toward your goal.  When you look at it from the point of view where you have five random cards, it's less likely that they will form a flush than a straight.  So, it's more difficult to even get the four-flush than the open-ended straight.\r\n\r\nThe odds for getting a flush are 508:1, and to get a straight it's 254:1.\r\n\r\nBecause flushes are less likely than straights, they're valued higher. Flushes are rarer than straights.\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poker_probability
