11298	2	6257	0b645531-cb29-48cb-a782-8dc1ecb9c29a	2015-09-15 21:08:50.657	1762	\N	\N	The pot is split to the lowest chip you have in play, typically a one dollar chip. That gives each player 33 dollars with a one dollar remainder. Typically this dollar is given to the player in the earliest position. \r\n\r\nSometimes the odd chip is given to the last player.\r\nSometimes the odd chip is given to the dealer.\r\nSometimes the odd chip is left in the middle to be played for in the next hand.\r\n\r\nYou can really do it any way you want, the important thing is that you always do it the same way in your game in the interest of fairness.
