11699	2	6399	102f4ff3-8368-491a-b021-a41fe26c4931	2015-11-03 18:39:04.337	3782	\N	\N	AA is the best starting hand in poker.  You should always play pre-flop.  You don't know what the other person has and statistically you beat all other hands pre-flop.  I've never and would never fold AA whether it's a tourney or cash game.  This is statistically the best starting hand pre-flop.  It doesn't matter whether you're on the bubble or not.  Play your hand. You asked about pre-flop.\r\n\r\nNow, after the flop is a different story.
