11856	2	6470	c9ddc5bd-7ede-4fdf-935d-2a29a63fb793	2015-11-27 00:52:37.72	3539	\N	\N	Although this can be a house-related regulation, it's always good to look at the official [TDA][1], if you read Rule 43, you'll find that the raiser must at least raise the ***"largest bet or raise of the current round"***.\r\n\r\nWell what does that mean? it means that if you want to re-raise the minimum, you need to look at how much was **added** to the calling amount during the previous raise, those **added** chips are your minimum raise, so you make your call and then add **those** chips.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\nSmall blind is $1, big bling is $2, the **first** raise must simply be double the last bet, which means "$4 to go". The next re-raiser can make it at least $6 because the previous raiser added $2 to his regular call, the next re-raiser looks at what the previous re-raiser did, he added $2 to his regular call of $4, so that's the minimum raise, $6 + $2 = $8 to go. And so on.\r\n\r\nHaving said all that, notice that the minimum raise usually gets called because of the lack of [fold equity][2].\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.pokertda.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/01/Poker-TDA-Rules-2015-Version-1.0-full-longform-PDF-1.pdf\r\n  [2]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fold_equity
11857	5	6470	5780e99d-8bc9-4170-80d1-d75376ae75db	2015-11-27 01:11:47.727	3539	\N	added 133 characters in body	Although this can be a house-related regulation, it's always good to look at the official [TDA][1], if you read Rule 43, you'll find that the raiser must at least raise the ***"largest bet or raise of the current round"***.\r\n\r\nWell what does that mean? it means that if you want to re-raise the minimum, you need to look at how much was **added** to the calling amount during the previous raise, those **added** chips are your minimum raise, so you make your call and then add **those** chips (make sure to do so in 'one move' as it's not allowed to [string bet][2]).\r\n\r\nExample:\r\nSmall blind is $1, big bling is $2, the **first** raise must simply be double the last bet, which means "$4 to go". The next re-raiser can make it at least "$6 to go" because the previous raiser added $2 to his regular call amount, the next re-raiser looks at what the previous re-raiser did, he added $2 to his regular call of $4, so that's the minimum raise, $6 + $2 = $8 to go. And so on.\r\n\r\nHaving said all that, notice that the minimum raise usually gets called because of the lack of [fold equity][3].\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.pokertda.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/01/Poker-TDA-Rules-2015-Version-1.0-full-longform-PDF-1.pdf\r\n  [2]: http://www.pokernews.com/pokerterms/string-bet.htm\r\n  [3]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fold_equity
