12248	2	6617	a8ee6628-ecb7-44d3-8697-01671a174302	2016-01-12 01:59:17.107	3964	\N	\N	PREFLOP: Raise to 5BB. \r\n\r\nIn fact the pot is 2+2+1+2= 7, you should put in at least 7 more to steal it, expecially when you are bluffing (for example with A5s or KTs) so up to 2+7= 9. I prefer 10.\r\n\r\nFLOP: Check. \r\n\r\nIn fact, as played, you should check your whole range in a 3 way. This hand is particularly good to do that since you really want to just check/call on the flop and check/fold the turn. You should do the same with an A of course, check/calling again on the turn. You can (or not) lead out on turn if everyone check.\r\n\r\nTURN: Bet. \r\n\r\nIn fact this is a standard CHECK with the whole range as played vs reg. Btw he is a fish thus you can bet/fold turn to get payed by some smaller pairs or 7, and check/fold river then. (NOTICE THAT now we are taking the worst option since we know he is a fish and we are HU and we stop balancing).
12249	2	6618	eb10248a-c1a1-4a78-8940-eda73993f0a9	2016-01-12 02:03:20.143	1478	\N	\N	**TL;DR: It's always the best five-card hand that wins at showdown.**\r\n\r\nWho wins? It depends.  The Five Card Rule applies.  You make the best hand you can from your two hole cards and the five board cards. Your opponent does the same with their cards.  The best hand wins.  If the hands are the same, then the pot is split.\r\n\r\n**First example:**\r\n\r\nYou: K&hearts;K&diamond;\r\n\r\nOpponent: Q&hearts;Q&diamond;\r\n\r\nThe board comes 5&hearts;5&spades;7&clubs;7&spades;A&clubs;\r\n\r\nYour best hand from the 7 available cards is K&hearts;K&diamond;7&clubs;7&spades;A&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYour opponent's best hand is Q&hearts;Q&diamond;7&clubs;7&spades;A&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYou have two pair, kings and sevens. Your opponent has two pair, queens and sevens. Your hand is best, so you win the pot.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Second example, using the same board cards but different hole cards:**\r\n\r\nYou: 4&hearts;4&diamond;\r\n\r\nOpponent: 3&hearts;3&diamond;\r\n\r\nThe board comes 5&hearts;5&spades;7&clubs;7&spades;A&clubs;\r\n\r\nYour best hand from the 7 available cards is 7&clubs;7&spades;5&hearts;5&spades;A&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYour opponent's best hand is also 7&clubs;7&spades;5&hearts;5&spades;A&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYou both have two pair, sevens and fives with an ace kicker, so you split the pot.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Third example:**\r\n\r\nIf one of your cards can play as the kicker (i.e., a single high card that plays in the set of five total cards), one player can still have the best hand even if the pocket pair is no good.  Say you both have the same hands from the previous example, but the final board card is a 2...\r\n\r\nYou: 4&hearts;4&diamond;\r\n\r\nOpponent: 3&hearts;3&diamond;\r\n\r\nThe board comes 5&hearts;5&spades;7&clubs;7&spades;2&clubs;\r\n\r\nYour best hand from the 7 available cards is 7&clubs;7&spades;5&hearts;5&spades;4&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYour opponent's best hand is also 7&clubs;7&spades;5&hearts;5&spades;3&clubs;.\r\n\r\nYou both have two pair, sevens and fives, but your 4 kicker is better than your opponent's 3, so you win the pot. (Pocket 3's happens to be the worst possible hand on this board.)\r\n\r\n\r\n**It's always the best five-card hand.**\r\n\r\n\r\n
12250	2	6619	eb66337e-cfbe-4a0f-9724-fc17978398f4	2016-01-12 02:04:54.66	3964	\N	\N	NO!\r\n\r\nFirst of all you have Fold Equity, so you can bet higher.\r\n\r\nSecond you should not change your sizing based on your hand... but based on the board. You can do that against fishes, you should not think too much about maths, just do the action you think exploits him. Against pros you can't tell them your hand with different sizing.\r\n\r\nThird, you should explain the whole hand, a generic situation makes no sense for a pro player.
12251	2	6620	18f57dae-cfb8-4336-937e-e47f8fd5cdc8	2016-01-12 02:14:52.18	3964	\N	\N	PREFLOP: call.\r\n\r\nStandard, too "deep".\r\n\r\nFLOP: check.\r\n\r\nStandard.\r\n\r\nTURN: shove.\r\n\r\nHonestly I don't think he is gonna check/pushing flop with FD that much, so he almost never has flash on turn, he probably has FD on turn with 1/2 overcards or pure bluff with random heart, your stack is too short this is not cash game, just PUSH.
