12424	2	6681	a49321e9-f008-4dc7-bf06-c19a87472269	2016-02-02 01:32:53.163	1762	\N	\N	Each player in a basic game of poker is given five cards to make their hand. There are variants to the game where players receive more then five cards and players have community cards. However it is the best five cards of a players hand that make their hand.\r\n\r\nIf the best five cards you have, are not better then another players best five cards you loose the pot. If your five best five cards are the same as another players best five cards you split the pot.   \r\n\r\nThe hand rankings for five card poker games.\r\n\r\n 1. Straight flushes\r\n 2. Four of a kind\r\n 3. Full Houses\r\n 4. Flushes\r\n 5. Straights\r\n 6. Three of a kind\r\n 7. Two pair\r\n 8. Pairs\r\n 9. High cards by rank\r\n\r\nSuites all rank the same. In other words no particular flush is better then another particular flush of the same five cards because one is of a particular suite.\r\n\r\nKickers only count when they are part of the best five cards. A better sixth card has no bearing whatsoever in determining a winning hand. \r\n\r\nWhatever the poker game is: **it is always the best five cards**. However there can be variations with community card games as to where those best five cards are.\r\n\r\nIn Texas Holdem all players have seven cards, the two hole cards in their hand and the five community cards that make up the board or flop. \r\n\r\nWith Omaha games your best five cards must consist of two cards in your hand and three cards on the board.\r\n\r\nIn other variants of poker such as five card draw, Seven card stud etc. Where you posses all your cards the best five cards rule still applies. \r\n\r\nThere are variants of poker that use other then the five card rule. Texas Holdem and Omaha do not use other then the five card rule.\r\n\r\nThere is no condition in a five card hand where you can win the pot based on your sixth or seventh card. There are no tie breakers unless your best five cards are better then your opponents best five cards. \r\n\r\nExamples are almost futile. There are virtually an unlimited number of hands possible. The best five cards of a hand are a simple formula of what the best five card in your hand are. It is very basic, if your confused it is because you are reading into it more then it entails. There can only be five best cards to make a hand and they either beat or tie your opponents best five cards.\r\n\r\nThe hand rankings list above in this post is truncated. To provide a perfectly granulated list would require several more hours of typing, you need to be able to fill in the blanks. (The best five cards)\r\n\r\nWhen both players have one pair or two pair you need to understand you go to kickers to determine the best five cards. You need to understand that only the highest straight wins, not the longest straight and that straights and flushes do not have kickers. You need to understand that sevens full of threes beat sevens full of deuces. You need to understand the basic differences between Omaha and Holdem, where one requires that you play two cards in your hand and the other does not.\r\n \r\nYou simply need to know it is the best five cards, nothing more and nothing less. You should also understand that the five card rule is an abstract rule that only covers certain forms of poker and that the other forms of poker have nothing to do with the five card rule.\r\n\r\nHere is some reference for you:\r\n\r\n[Wikipedia list of poker hands][1]\r\n\r\n[Wikipedia Poker][2]\r\n\r\nBook recommendations\r\n\r\n[Poker for dummies][3]\r\n\r\n[Poker: How to play poker and other gambling games][4]\r\n\r\n[Fundamentals of Poker][5]\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_poker_hands\r\n  [2]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poker\r\n  [3]: http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/0764552325?ref_=cm_lmf_img_3\r\n  [4]: http://www.amazon.com/How-Play-Poker-Other-Gambling/dp/0600609227/ref=pd_sim_14_5?ie=UTF8&dpID=51j19UN2GCL&dpSrc=sims&preST=_AC_UL160_SR112%2C160_&refRID=1XP1K89X4HMVEREM4PXZ\r\n  [5]: http://www.amazon.com/Fundamentals-Poker-Lynne-Loomis/dp/1880685248/ref=pd_sim_14_12?ie=UTF8&dpID=515cmgyk2KL&dpSrc=sims&preST=_AC_UL160_SR99%2C160_&refRID=1XP1K89X4HMVEREM4PXZ
12425	2	6682	54283947-dab4-47d8-a54c-364cc8aab8db	2016-02-02 10:22:10.983	3876	\N	\N	<h1>Hands Overview</H1>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Straight Flush</li>\r\n<li>Four of a kind</li>\r\n<li>Full house</li>\r\n<li>Flush</li>\r\n<li>Straight</li>\r\n<li>Three of a kind</li>\r\n<li>Two Pair</li>\r\n<li>Pair</li>\r\n<li>High card</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h3>Why that order?</h3>\r\nThe order is based on math / statistics.  It is simply <i>harder</i> to make one hand versus another.\r\n\r\n<H1>Hole cards</H1> \r\nThe cards in your hand.  In hold-em two cards.\r\n\r\n<H1>Board</H1> \r\nBoard is the common / shared cards.\r\n\r\n<H1>Best five cards</H1> \r\nEvery hand is exactly five cards. Between your hole cards and board make your best hand. You may play the board. \r\n\r\n<H1>Rank</H1> \r\nRank is Ace through 2.  For identical hands the higher rank wins.  \r\n\r\n<H1>Suit</H1> \r\nSuit is spade, club, heart, or diamond.  The are equal.     \r\n\r\n<H1>Kicker</H1> \r\nKicker is a single card. Kicker only comes into play when the main part of the hand is not five cards and can tie. Three of a kind is not five cards but you cannot have a tie (in a clean deck).\r\n\r\n<H1>Nuts</H1> \r\nBased on the board (common cards) you have the best possible hand.  <i>In most  tournament play you are required to raise on the river if you have the nuts.</i> \r\n\r\n\r\n<H1>Tie / Split</H1> \r\nYes you can have a tie and you split the pot.\r\n\r\n<h3>1 Straight Flush</H3> \r\nFive sequential cards of the same suit.  \r\nAnnounced:  X high straight flush  \r\n\r\n<h3>2 Four of a kind</H3> \r\nFour cards of the same rank.  \r\nAnnounced:  X quads or X four of a kind\r\n\r\n<h3>3 Full house</H3> \r\nThree cards of the same rank and two card of same rank.  Also called a boat.  The three determines the high.  88855 beats 44499.  \r\nAnnounced:  X over Y (where the X the three)\r\n\r\n<h3>4 Flush</H3> \r\nFive cards of the same suit.  The top card determines the best.  A6543 beats KQJ98.   \r\nAnnounced:  X high flush\r\n\r\n<h3>5 Straight</H3> \r\nFive sequential cards. Ace is both high and low.  Ace through 5 is often called a wheel.  Ace through 10 is often called Broadway.   \r\nAnnounced:  X high straight\r\n\r\n<h3>6 Three of a kind</H3> \r\nThree cards of the same rank.  \r\nAnnounced:  X trip or X set or Three of kind X\r\n\r\n<h3>7 Two Pair</H3> \r\nTwo cards of the same rank and two cards of the same rank.  If both pair are the same rank then it is four of a kind.  The top pair wins.  Top pair can tie so in that case the lower pair is the tie breaker.  And if both pair tie you go to the kicker.   \r\nAnnounced:  X up   \r\nUp versus Over is the distinction in announcing two pair versus boat. \r\n\r\n<h3>8 Pair</H3> \r\nTwo cards of the same rank. If tie you go the kicker.  2nd or 3rd kicker if required.   \r\nAnnounced:  Pair X or Xs\r\n\r\n<h3>9 High card</H3> \r\nHigh card. If tie you go the kicker. 2nd, 3rd, or 4th kicker if required.   \r\nAnnounced:  X high *with an intonation of I hope it holds up*\r\n \r\n
