e draw, and 91.1157% chance of total loss on the draw.\r\n\r\nSo .0657% more chance for total win, .0657% more chance for total loss, .1313% less chance for chopped pot.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBasically, running multiple times with reshuffle slightly increases the hand variance relative to running multiple times with no reshuffle.  If you're playing to not lose everything, run it multiple times, but you tradeoff a chance at a bigger payday.\r\n 
12491	5	6700	63278c96-a134-4152-8b66-ae49c0bb984a	2016-02-05 15:04:27.037	3876	\N	added 51 characters in body	Pick is it 8 or 10   \r\n\r\nAt 8 I think it is 0.4114  \r\nOr \r\nThis is for exactly one ace out - (not two)\r\n\r\nUsing [combination][1]\r\n\r\n(2/1) * (48/13) / (50/14)  \r\n\r\n(2 aces need 1)  (48 non ace need 13) / (50 cards need 14)\r\n\r\nBoth other aces out would be 0.0743\r\n\r\nAdd them for 1 or 2 aces out = 0.4857\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nwe need mathjax on this site  \r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combination
