12574	2	6728	f840ffd7-2bf0-448c-a1c7-f6dab79c22fa	2016-02-12 19:04:58.187	3876	\N	\N	The way to approach this is [binomial coefficient][1] / [combination][2]\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binomial_coefficient\r\n  [2]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combination\r\n\r\nYou have two cards  \r\n50 cards remaining   \r\nThe number of 2 card combination in 50 is 1,225 \r\n(50/2) = 1,225  \r\n\r\nLet's say you did not have a blocker aces (e.g. you had QQ)  \r\nThe number of ways to make AA(2) from 4 is  \r\n(4/2) = 6 (sc, sh, sd, ch, cd, dh)  \r\nThe odd are 6 / 1,225 = 0.0049 = 203 : 1  \r\n\r\nLet's say you have AK so you have block on each  \r\nThe number of ways to make AA from 3 is  \r\n(3/2) = 3  \r\nThe odd are 3 / 1,225 = 0.00245 = 407 : 1  \r\n\r\nSo with a single blocker you cut the odds of facing AA by 2 \r\n\r\nAA or KK is just additive as those hands are mutually exclusive    \r\nThe change of AA or KK is   \r\n0.0049 = 203 : 1  \r\n\r\nYour chance of facing AA or KK is exactly the same if you are holding QQ or AK  \r\n\r\nI know not the question but interesting   \r\nFor stuff like this is why you need to use combinations     \r\nWhat is the chance of facing AA, KK, or AK    \r\nHolding QQ then   \r\n(8/2) = 28   \r\nThe odd are 28 / 1,225 = 0.0229 = 42.75 : 1      \r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n
12636	2	6751	9f851d1b-e645-4075-bace-c4dac949ad2b	2016-02-20 03:52:45.333	3876	\N	\N	 - player 1   \r\nK:hearts:Q:diamonds:  \r\n - player 2   \r\n4:hearts:3:hearts: \r\n - board    \r\nQ:hearts:6:hearts:5:spades:3:diamonds:\r\n\r\nplayer 1 is ahead    \r\nplayer 2 must improve but player 1 can improve also   \r\n\r\na flush or straight for player 2 wins out right   \r\n8 hearts + 7 straight = 15 outs  \r\n52 - 8 = 44 cards out  \r\nwin flush or straight = 15 / (44-15) = 15 / 29 = 0.5172\r\n  \r\nbut player 2 could draw a 4 for two pair - 3 outs     \r\nbut a K or Q for player 1 would kill it - 5 outs   \r\n3 / (44-3) * (1 - 5/(43-5)) = 0.0635\r\n\r\nplayer 2 could draw a 3 for trips - 2 outs   \r\nbut a Q for player 1 would kill it - 2 outs     \r\n2 / (44-2) * (1 - 2/(43-2) = 0.0453  \r\n\r\n**total player 2 = 0.626**\r\n\r\n**total player 1** = 1 - player 2 = **0.374**\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n 
