12749	2	6793	4f2f6076-5152-40dd-b463-b3e4a9d21e28	2016-03-03 02:55:27.027	3876	\N	\N	What is in the middle is called the pot  \r\nIf someone bets $5 into a $10 pot the pot is now $15   \r\nSo facing the bet I am getting $15/$5 pot odd = **3:1**   \r\nI am risking $5 to win $15   \r\n\r\nWhat people can miss on pot odds is if you win you get your bet back  \r\nSo if I call 3 times and win once I am even  \r\n-5$    \r\n-5$ \r\n-5$    \r\n+$15 -5$ +5$  \r\nNet = 0  \r\n\r\nI get you want to look at this as weights and averages but that is not the right look.  Get a book on poker math. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n 
