12795	2	6806	d3705a3d-626c-4624-b834-5b865a81688f	2016-03-08 19:03:15.23	3876	\N	\N	To me there is nothing magic.  And there is no mathematical proof on how to play a tournament. \r\n\r\nWhen you look at your stack look at how many orbits you have left.  Have some enter the pot practices based on number of orbits left.  If the blinds will go to go up before you get there then that should go into your current orbits left calculation.    \r\n\r\nPot odds take care of them self.  If you put in a pot size raise in early position then do so.  Ante or not will effect starting pot size - all that really matters is pre-betting pot size. \r\n\r\nBase your strategy on position, cards, pot size, and orbits.    \r\nWhen the binds go up the strategy is the same - just pot size and number of orbits left changes  \r\n\r\nClearly pay out structure comes into play but that is separate.\r\n\r\n
