12854	2	6822	a31ee639-c50e-41a7-af6e-0d4ce17ec92b	2016-03-13 21:07:15.853	3876	\N	\N	The answer is that you need immediate pot odds.  There is absolutely NO basis to assume they are going to let up on the turn if a blank hits.  \r\n\r\nAccording to Skansky every time you make an opponent make a bad decision you benefit.  Opponent gave you 3:1 and you called thinking you would get a free card on the river.  Any good opponent is going to turn up the heat if a blank hits on the turn.\r\n\r\nIf opponent had nothing and really wanted you gone they would bet the pot.  \r\n\r\nThat is a value bet if they had a pair or better and were protecting from the  flush a better bet is actuality 1/2 the pot as you probably would have chased that also getting 2:1 thinking you would get a free river.  \r\n\r\nLets look at EV of villain  \r\nOn the turn take down the pot with a pot sized bet  \r\n(this assume you will fold to a pot sized bet)   \r\nEV 800  \r\n\r\nBet 1/2 the pot and get a call on the flop - pot is now 1600   \r\nIf a blank hits bet 1/2 the pot again and take it down on the turn  \r\nEV = -400 + (1 - 9/43)1600 = 865  \r\n865 > 100 \r\nIf villain had a single of the suit and took your outs to 8 then 902  \r\n\r\nBy only betting 1/3 the pot on the flop villain actually had a negative EV if the plan was to take down a blank on the turn 600 versus 590.\r\n\r\nIf your ace is good then you pick up 3 more outs.  So I think you did the right thing to call getting 3:1.  You are getting just short of 3:1 on the turn alone if the Ace is good (they only have a single pair and no ace).\r\n\r\nAce little is just not that strong. You only want to play it late and cheap in multiplayer pots. You are only going to make a flush by the river 1:16. And if you pair you ace you can easily get yourself in trouble.  A lot of people will say mid suited connectors are better to play than ace little suited.\r\n\r\nThat was just poorly sized value bet by villain.  It would be like top pair or trips that wanted to keep mid or bottom pair along on a board with no draws.\r\n\r\n\r\n
