12916	5	6842	af1dd418-da0b-4573-97f0-1ea6a2bfb3ed	2016-03-18 21:27:33.517	3876	\N	added 157 characters in body	Using [combinations][1]  \r\nI will use combin(n,k) as that is the syntax in excel  \r\nBuy board you mean the 5 cards up?   \r\n\r\n4*combin(13,4)*48 / combin(52,5)  = 0.0528 = 5.3% = 18:1  \r\n\r\nabove includes full flushes     \r\nit ignores the cards in your hand as you did not state if you were a card to the suit or not  \r\n\r\nexactly 4 is   \r\n4*combin(13,4)*39 / combin(52,5)  = 0.0429 = 4.3% = 22:1  \r\n\r\nexactly 5 is what you see as the odds of a flush  \r\n4*combin(13,5) / combin(52,5) = 0.00198 = 0.198% = 504:1   \r\nthis includes a straight flush  \r\n\r\nmake flush on the river from a suited hand   \r\ncombin(11,3) * combine(47,2) / combin(50,5) = 0.08418 = 8.42% = 10.9:1  \r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combination
12942	2	6850	bcebfb3c-2cdf-4622-81b9-818ff64f0ccc	2016-03-21 20:45:38.627	3876	\N	\N	The odds of you getting a boat are [2.60%][1] \r\n\r\nFrom the boat there are 45 cards out (52 - 2 - 5)  \r\nThe only way for you to get quaded is for the other hand to match the pair on the boat    \r\nSo the odds of getting quadded are:  \r\n[(2/2) / (45/2)][2] = 0.00101 = 0.1%  \r\nWhich also = 2/45 * 1/44\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poker_probability\r\n  [2]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combination
