13120	2	6908	a40fdbdb-2c16-45fa-8e58-d3d47f927945	2016-04-19 05:19:30.883	1762	\N	\N	The exact probability that the opponent holds a jack is rather irrelevant at this point in the hand, without considering things like how the hand has gone down to this point. If the player had just cautiously called a bet on the flop then check raises the turn you can give him a higher probability of holding a jack for example.\r\n\r\nThe fact that two of the jacks are on board of course means there are less jacks for player to hold, but that is really not a consideration when your trying to figure out if an opponent holds a jack.
