13370	2	6998	89b7e421-7a1c-4a19-9c12-3767428a2115	2016-05-27 16:02:26.223	3876	\N	\N	Not saying I agree 100% but this is from Phil Gordon's Little Green Book  \r\nThis is only for first to act   \r\n\r\nearly  \r\n2.5bb - 3.0bb  \r\n\r\nmiddle  \r\n3.0bb - 3.5bb \r\n\r\nlate  \r\n3.5bb - 4.0bb  \r\n\r\nsmall blind   \r\n3.0bb \r\n\r\nHis argument is commit fewer chips out of position     \r\nBut he also says to only play premium hands out of position     \r\nYou are not trying to steal blinds in early position     \r\n\r\nIn late position you are also tying to steal blinds so you need to apply pressure   \r\n\r\nHe advocates set preflop bet / raise so you don't advertise your hand or if you are on a steal   \r\n\r\nHe says on some tables you may need to move the numbers up of down \r\n\r\nI certainly don't agree with your raise 2.5 in late position   \r\nThat is not much pressure on the blinds to fold as they already have the bet partially covered   \r\nBB pot odd are  (2.5 + .5 + 1) / 1.5 = 4 / 1.5 = 8 : 3  \r\nEven two under to two over is 3 : 2  \r\nThe only thing you are pricing out is an over pair at 4 : 1   \r\nIf I really do have an over pair and get looked up then I want more money in the pot  \r\n\r\nAlso from early position you are more likely to get popped (re-raised) so if you are on AA you can push to take the pot down / isolate or slow play. 
