14551	2	8063	b7392efd-6b1e-4bb4-b47c-bf7f9da006de	2016-06-30 00:47:57.46	4361	\N	\N	The most reliable known method to detect whether an online poker site gives itself an *edge* or *rigs* the game on a certain way is to take a huge amount of data and analyze it against the odds, look for a trend. It would take hundreds of thousands of hands worth of data before the statistics show any kind of variation from expected results due to the randomness factor.\r\n\r\nThe accepted answer of [this possible duplicate question][1] summarizes this well.\r\n\r\nAnother method would be if you actually got your hands on their algorithm and deciphered it which would probably require some legally questionable activity in itself... but this would be hard evidence. Not to get too side-tracked but there are a lot of gray areas when it comes to accessing information so there are legal exceptions.\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://poker.stackexchange.com/questions/413/what-to-do-if-we-suspect-online-poker-server-is-cheating?rq=1
