14641	2	8086	681b5c4c-6b52-408e-a05a-0a5d4d323228	2016-07-15 16:56:48.457	3876	\N	\N	You are not providing enough information.  All we know is cards.  It is not clear if you had position.  What is *huge* bet on river?  \r\n\r\nOn the flop you have nothing but Ace high and a gut shot straight draw. There is no reason to build a pot here.  Your Ace has some show down value.  If you call the flush cards dead you only have 5 outs (3 3s and 2 Aces).\r\n\r\nIf villain got in late and for a good price that is in their range.  If villain was BB he got in for 3:1.  If villain is on a flush draw they have more outs.  If you try and price them out then you have priced yourself out.  \r\n\r\nBe happy villain checked the flop.  You did not improve on turn.  8 could have hit the villain.  Be glad villain checked.  \r\n\r\nYou got worse possible river.  A bet of 2.5X the pot is nuts or a stone cold bluff.  Would they play flush draw that way - the answer is yes.  Just release.  It would need to be 5/12 chance that is bluff to even break even calling.  Only a maniac bluffs that much.\r\n\r\nWhy did you even call 4BB from mid preflop with A5o?\r\n\r\n
