14941	2	8190	0421958f-30d9-4c1e-83f6-5d3580900629	2016-08-16 15:19:43.017	3876	\N	\N	Your chance of a suited hole cards is 12 / 51 = 0.235294118  \r\nJust short of 1/4  \r\n\r\n<h2>Opponent same flush - two cards</h2>  \r\ncombin(11,2) / combine(50,2) = 0.029387755  \r\n\r\nChance you make a flush by the river = 0.043317075 = 22.1 : 1  \r\n\r\n<h2>Opponent same flush - one card</h2>  \r\nLet say one card and T or greater  \r\nYou are playing 89s  \r\n\r\nOpponent chance = 5*39/50 = 0.16  \r\nThat is random  \r\n\r\nIf your opponent is only playing A-T = then 0.40 chance they have single flush (higher than you)   \r\nWell pair are also in their range - but then they can make a boat to beat your flush so that is about a wash     \r\n\r\nYou are going to make flush with the board only showing 3   \r\nYou are safe there cannot be an over flush  \r\n0.044 = 21.63   \r\nThat number make sense as they say suited adds about 4%.\r\n\r\nWhat are the chances of a 4 or 5 flush on the board   \r\n0.0048 = 207 : 1    \r\nYou are in a situation of getting beat by a single card \r\n\r\nNot going to face 4 or 5 flush on the board often but if you do be cautions - there is about a 40% chance you are beat if you range your opponent to A-T    \r\nBet hard when the board hits 3   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n
