14996	5	8200	901986fe-53bf-48f9-92bb-ecbc016ead5d	2016-08-22 23:01:26.117	3876	\N	deleted 112 characters in body	First let's begin with the probability that there are 5 different-suited pocket pairs dealt in one hand:\r\n\r\n( 78/(52 choose 2) ) * ( 72/(50 choose 2) ) * ( 66/(48 choose 2) ) * ( 60/(46 choose 2) ) * ( 54/(44 choose 2) )  = **.000000669415**\r\n\r\n\r\nNext, we find the probability that EACH OF THE FIVE pocket pairs is matched on the board, making five three-of-a-kinds:\r\n\r\n.000000669415 * (2/42) * (2/41) * (2/40) * (2/39) * (2/38) * 5! = **.0000000000251817**\r\n\r\n\r\nSo the odds of this hand happening are about **1 in 40,000,000,000**.  \r\n\r\nSome other interesting events with better odds:\r\n\r\n - Odds of being killed by lightning: 2,320,000 to 1 \r\n - Odds of having identical quadruplets: 15,000,000 to 1\r\n - Odds of dying by a vending machine: 112,000,000 to 1\r\n - Odds of winning the Powerball: 292,000,000 to 1\r\n - Odds of being killed on a 5-mile bus trip: 500,000,000 to 1 \r\n\r\n\r\n[source][1] [source][2]\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.thedailybeast.com/articles/2012/03/30/15-things-more-likely-to-happen-than-winning-mega-millions.html\r\n  [2]: http://www.funny2.com/odds.htm
