15414	2	8347	c02cd2e3-e03a-41f7-acfd-ee8214696cc5	2016-10-24 18:27:35.127	3876	\N	\N	EV = 0 = b*3 - (1-b)*1   \r\n0 = 4b - 1  \r\nb = 1/4    \r\n\r\nbluff rate is always 1 / (pot odds + 1)  \r\n\r\nwhat if they bet 5x pot    \r\npot odds (1 + 5)/5 = 6/5    \r\nEV = 0 = b*6 - (1-b)*5   \r\n0 = 11b - 5  \r\nb = 5 / 11 \r\n1 / (6/5 + 1) = 1 / (11/5) = 5 / 11    \r\n\r\nwhat if they bet 100x pot    \r\npot odds (1 + 100)/100 = 101/100    \r\nEV = 0 = b*101 - (1-b)*100   \r\n0 = 201b - 100  \r\nb = 100 / 101  ~ 1/2  \r\nThe math does not change that much from 5x pot bet to a 100x  \r\nIt is about intimidation     \r\n\r\nPO  BR  \r\n1 = 1/2   \r\n2 = 1/3  \r\n3 = 1/4  \r\n4 = 1/5  
