15428	2	8350	206aa051-395b-4865-8b58-bcd759d11f2c	2016-10-25 23:36:19.633	4700	\N	\N	Ideally, you should notify the dealer that you can see the other player's hand. If someone were able to prove that you were able to see the other player's hand it may be considered evidence of [Collusion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheating_in_poker#Collusion). In reality, it's easy to deny that you saw the other player's hand, so you are free to keep looking as long as you are not obvious about it. It's each player's responsibility to protect their hand.
