15570	2	8406	7cbe27e5-3de5-44f8-98a9-6e9e73fac322	2016-11-06 19:45:19.63	3876	\N	\N	<h2>Convert Odds to Percentage</h2>\r\nOdds are always with a :  \r\n1:1  \r\n2:1  \r\n3:1      \r\nPercentage / fraction    \r\n33% = 1/3   \r\n50% = 1/2   \r\n\r\npercentage = 1 / (odds + 1)   \r\nodds = 100 / percentage - 1\r\n\r\n<h2>Pot Odds</h2>\r\nPot size : amount you have to call  \r\n$100 pot and call $20  = 5 : 1  \r\nThe $100 includes the raise you are calling - that bet is in the pot  \r\nYou are risking $1 to win $5   \r\n\r\n<h2>Hand Odds</h2>\r\n(cards left - outs)/outs   \r\nIf you have 8 outs on the turn then  \r\n(46-8)/8 = 4.75 : 1  \r\n\r\n<h2>Pot Odds Versus Hand Odds</h2> \r\nIf you are getting   \r\nPot Odds > Hand Odds (4:75) then call  \r\nReward > Risk  \r\n\r\nPot Odds (5:1) > Hand Odds (4:75) then you are getting immediate odds to call  \r\n\r\nIf the bet was 1/2 the pot giving you 3:1 pot odds then you should not call 8 outs (unless you think you are getting good implied odds)  \r\n\r\n*Percentage is covered in the other answer*  \r\n\r\n
