15686	2	8443	5c717df1-a8ab-4cd8-948c-ea612ce25735	2016-11-22 17:08:46.6	937	\N	\N	The chance of a full house is the same whether you draw one or two. Drawing two slightly increases your chance of quads. Drawing one is more deceptive--it will generally cause your opponent to put you on two pair, so he'll be more likely to call with his own two pair.\r\n\r\nOf course it depends on the situation, the players, the other rules, and so on; but generally speaking, 5-card-draw players draw one to trips, because the deception is worth more than the increased chance of quads.
