15698	2	8450	037dc596-791d-4226-95fb-7d3a3c5d0788	2016-11-25 11:37:03.997	4771	\N	\N	`Kd 3s` beats `7c 7s` on a `Ad Xd Xd Xd Xd` board, you are correct.\r\n\r\nThe player with `Kd 3s` has `Ad Kd Xd Xd Xd`, an A-K high flush.\r\n\r\nThe player with `7c 7s` has `Ad Xd Xd Xd Xd`, an A-X high flush (and X can never be greater than K in this example.\r\n\r\nAs you suggest, it's all about the best 5 card hand, so '2d 3s' vs '7c 7s' on a `Ad Td 6d 4d 3d` board for example would be a chop, because the `2d` in the player's hand does not improve their flush - both players have a 5 card hand of `Ad Td 6d 4d 3d`.
15713	5	8450	aa88be1e-fa7d-4d20-aafa-a895a6f2432e	2016-11-27 22:02:42.31	4771	\N	edited body	`Kd 3s` beats `7c 7s` on a `Ad Xd Xd Xd Xd` board, you are correct.\r\n\r\nThe player with `Kd 3s` has `Ad Kd Xd Xd Xd`, an A-K high flush.\r\n\r\nThe player with `7c 7s` has `Ad Xd Xd Xd Xd`, an A-X high flush (and X can never be greater than K in this example.\r\n\r\nAs you suggest, it's all about the best 5 card hand, so `2d 3s` vs `7c 7s` on a `Ad Td 6d 4d 3d` board for example would be a chop, because the `2d` in the player's hand does not improve their flush - both players have a 5 card hand of `Ad Td 6d 4d 3d`.
