15864	5	8396	8073373e-f44b-4c0d-a012-3c1b7d6df4ed	2016-12-13 13:09:29.823	4771	\N	cleaned up body of post, spelling grammar and details	Click [here](http://www.boomplayer.com/en/poker-hands/Boom/21363651_931E355A62) to see the hand in [Stars Boom Hand Player](http://www.boomplayer.com).\r\n\r\nIn the early stages (Level 3, 25/50/A6) of a turbo full-ring tournament, I have 1,082 in my stack and get dealt J&hearts;T&hearts; in the CO. Action is folded to me and I raise to 2.5x (125), villain (who has me covered with over 1,600 in his stack) calls from the SB and we go heads up to the flop.\r\n\r\nThe flop comes K&diamond;J&clubs;J&spades;, so I'm pretty happy and after villain checks, I c-bet half pot (177 into 354) and get called. At this point I think he's either slow-playing something like `AA`, `KK`, `AK`, or any `J`, or he's trying to catch me with a weak pair / draw like `AQ`, `QQ`, `QT`, `TT`. I rule out bluffs because he called pre-flop out of position.\r\n\r\nThe turn card is 6&clubs; and he check-minraises my 35% (250 into 708) bet. I don't think he has any draws at this point, so i'm pretty scared of a `J` with better kicker and `KK`. I even think _maaybe_ he got there with `66` somehow. \r\n\r\nTo be honest though, I don't think he gives me credit for a `J`, so I think it's plausible he's got `AA`, `AK`, `KQ`, and even some weaker hands like `KT`, `JT` or `J9s`. I can't really calculate what percentage of hands I beat, but the price is about 35%, so I'm thinking I have to call, so I do.\r\n\r\nThe river is the 4&diamond; - he shoves (he has me covered and I have 274 behind) and I can't really fold holding 14% of the pot.\r\n\r\nHe turns A&diamond;J&diamond; and takes the pot, kicking me out of the tournament.\r\n_______\r\n\r\nK&diamond;J&clubs;J&spades;6&clubs;4&diamond;\r\n\r\nH: J&hearts;T&hearts;\r\nV: A&diamond;J&diamond;\r\n\r\nIs this just a bad beat or did I make any mistakes here? Should I have checked the turn keeping the pot small? Could I really fold after the check-raise on the turn? Was my read poor, i.e. could I have narrowed his range to only hands that beat me? Was there a way to scare him into thinking I was holding KK? Is there any lesson to take from this?
