16227	5	112	aae4e88d-c046-43f3-b889-df0f6ba297b4	2017-01-12 21:50:50.637	4771	\N	added clarification and some additional detail	Texas Hold'Em is a community-card poker variant in which each player receives 2 cards face down (known as their "hole cards").\r\n\r\nA "flop" of 3 cards is then dealt face up, followed by a single face-up card (the turn), and a final face-up card (the river). The best 5 card poker hand, using any of the player's 2 cards and the 5 community cards, wins. \r\n\r\nThere is a round of betting after the deal, and after the flop, turn, and river - 4 rounds of betting in total. The game can be played with fixed-limit, spread-limit, pot-limit and no-limit betting structures, with no-limit being the most common.\r\n\r\nTexas Hold'em is the most popular poker variant in the world.
