16281	2	8626	a3355d99-6bea-4615-852d-400452740eb3	2017-01-15 23:01:46.653	3876	\N	\N	Exploits on shuffle due to random rare.\r\n\r\nThe sites that have been exploited is due to off by one (they failed to shuffle the last or first card).\r\n\r\nNot uniform.  Arbitrary shuffles that just swap positions are not typically uniform.  A aviation of 7 is the common total on a roll of two dice.  \r\n\r\nThe [Fisher-Yates][1] shuffle is proven to be uniform and it is efficient.  It only requires 2601 random numbers.  You would need to know the existing deck and also the next 2601 ransom number to know the next shuffle.  You could know the top card by knowing the next single random if the loop is forward.  For that reason the shuffle is typically from the back.   \r\n\r\n    -- To shuffle an array a of n elements (indices 0..n-1):\r\n    for i from n−1 downto 1 do\r\n         j ← random integer such that 0 ≤ j ≤ i\r\n         exchange a[j] and a[i]\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisher%E2%80%93Yates_shuffle
