16333	5	8630	94127346-a2fd-43be-8adb-fe29a8148b92	2017-01-19 18:01:55.11	3876	\N	added 5 characters in body	Immediate odds to call a single bet/raise is not the same as overall pot odds. \r\n\r\nCount the number of players in the pot.  3 players the overall pot odds is 2:1 (plus any overlays from folded hands).\r\n\r\nYou were getting 9:2 on the first call so it looks very attractive if the was a limp and a mid raise.  But betting is not capped.  I think you need to release. \r\nIf you call you would likely get re-raised.  At that point you are likely up against bigger suited overs, AK, or over pairs.  You are a 4:1 dog and have to pay more to see a river.  Even if you hit then it is hard to get paid off.
16334	2	8641	10f3266c-0d33-40ef-aa25-ac14e730beed	2017-01-19 18:13:59.487	3876	\N	\N	Not going to accept my own answer for please post.  \r\n\r\nYou are out of position but you are closing betting.   If betting was still open no way I call.    \r\n\r\nWhat I look at first is odd to get a 4 flush or open ended straight draw on the flop.  They are not likely to let you see the turn for free.   \r\n\r\nYou are only getting a 8+ outs on flop about 5% of the time.  \r\n\r\nAssume by magic if you 8+ you are going to complete just to see if best case you should call.\r\n\r\nWhat are the pot odds  13 / 3.   Not even close to 95 / 5.\r\n\r\nHow much more would you need to get out of them IF you hit  \r\n\r\nEV = -3 + 1/20(16 + more) = 0    \r\n3 x 20 = 16 + more       \r\n60 - 16 = 44     \r\nBetween the two of them there are barely enough chips in play  \r\nNo way   \r\n\r\nLets see if it even works with 4    \r\nEV = -3 + 1/20(25 + more) = 0    \r\n60 - 25 = 35 = more     \r\n\r\nHow many chips in play = 4 x 25 = 100     \r\nYou would have to pick up 1/3 the chips in play and on top of that you are only going to complete the draw about 1/3 of the time    \r\nI don't think you can play this with even with 4 (small) raises in the pot  \r\nNot sure you could even play this with 100 BB behind     \r\n\r\nThe moral to the story is don't limp and let the BB play for free      \r\n\r\n   \r\n\r\n
