16417	2	8666	0d594500-8e40-4a80-be88-88973c83a07b	2017-01-25 05:49:18.85	4461	\N	\N	Most of the time  in poker, the WSOP rules are held as canon, so keeping that in mind, this is what the 2016 WSOP rulebook has to say:\r\n> 84. Non-Standard Folds: Any time before the end of the last betting round of a hand, folding in turn when there’s been no bet to you (ex: facing a check or first to act post-flop) or folding out of turn are both binding folds and may be subject to penalty in accordance with Rules 40 & 111. \r\n\r\nSo, yes, it is binding, and if done on purpose, grounds for the infringing player to be penalized.\r\n
