16658	2	8742	e5c97afd-6f1b-490a-9ee2-9baa5a40b2ee	2017-02-23 13:25:34.773	5026	\N	\N	Both players have the exact same hand, so it’s a pot split.\r\n\r\nTo determine who won, you need to choose the 5 best cards among the 7 possible cards for each player (2 from their hole cards, 5 from the community cards)\r\n\r\nleft player has a pair of tens made from the ten in his hole cards and the ten in the community cards, and a pair of kings from the community cards.\r\nYou then need to choose the best card from the remaining cards that you didn’t use to make a pair, which is the 8 in the community cards.\r\n\r\nRight player has the exact same two pairs has left player (same explanation). \r\nThis player also has an 8 in his hole cards, but this card cannot be used to make a pair with the 8 in the community cards because 6 cards would have to be used.\r\nSo this player just has to choose the remaining best cards, which is either their own 8 or the community 8.\r\n\r\nThe kickers in this example (7 for the left player, 8 for the right player) are not relevant, as the community cards provide a better card for the 5th card they have to choose.\r\n\r\n
