16763	2	8777	a0883d4d-9655-4232-8d31-872633c323ed	2017-03-05 18:18:06.91	5050	\N	\N	While technically not being ''the nuts'', this term is often used when someone smashes the flop and is unlikely to be behind. \r\n\r\nIn this case A8 should be miles ahead of your opponents range and you should be looking to get some value from Ax, 8x, A2 and maybe some other hands. Of course sets will still beat you, but you cannot be afraid for the monster under the bed. There are plenty of worse hands your opponent will call you with, besides you block most sets. To conclude, yes this hand should definitely be played as the winner here. If you only play sets like a winner in this spot, you really underplay your range, since sets are an extremely small percentage of your range. And ultimately, especially against experienced players, you will get pushed out of the pot way too often.
