16880	2	8816	7121127a-fbb1-43f9-923a-2e56454fb4e6	2017-03-17 20:25:50.11	3876	\N	\N	Villain goes all in every hand   \r\n\r\nSay blinds are 1, 2 and you start with 200 (100 bb)  \r\n\r\nIt would seem safe to just wait for AA but the problem there is getting blinded off.  If you wait 110 orbits you have paid 330.  Most likely you will hit AA in 1/2 that for 150.  But you still go broke as with 50 you double up to 100 and are behind where you started.   \r\n\r\nSo for sure you need to pick a range that that you will hit in 200 / 3 orbits = 66. In average you will hit in 1/2 that but why take a chance.  Step  back and pick a hand in the top 1 / 50.   The chance of not hitting that is 1 - (49/50)^122 = 91.5%.  The problem you have is if you open the range to bring that down then you increase the chance of loosing it when you play.  \r\n\r\nTop 5% hands is 88+,AJs+,KQs,AKo for equity against a random hand of 73%.  \r\n\r\nYour chance of winning is 0.915 * 0.73 = .66   \r\n\r\nBut wait that is not all you need to win more than once     \r\nOn average you are going to get blinded off 125 so you and only play for 75    \r\nSo you need to win 2 in a row 2/3 * 2/3 = 4/9    \r\nYou are a dog   \r\n\r\nBasically you need to pick a range that will survive back to back more than 1/2 of the time.  .7. * .7 = .49.   But you are still not guaranteed to hit before you are blinded out so top 1/4 hands.\r\n\r\nHit in 122 hands is basically 100%   \r\n\r\nPlay top 70% unfortunately you lose 40%. \r\n\r\nLose back to back is 16%.  \r\n\r\nSo you are an 84% favorite by playing    55+,A2s+,K5s+,Q7s+,J8s+,T8s+,98s,A7o+,A5o,K9o+,Q9o+,J9o+,T9o  \r\n\r\n
