17063	2	8869	4f98c165-da71-47b6-bc3e-9314611ec8c2	2017-04-08 20:13:18.487	3876	\N	\N	AKo plays better than AQo\r\n\r\nPre why do you raise for 6 BB?  It makes playing a lot hands expensive.\r\n\r\nShe sat out 5 hands and then called a pretty big bet.  You don't know much about her but she is is probably on a good hand.  You can rule out mid suited connectors that might call a small raise.  \r\n\r\nGood flop for you. You are only behind AK, 99, 88. $20 into $27 is a pretty big bet. Not that many hands that you ahead of would call. AJ, AT, KK, QQ, JJ, TT would call it off.  If you are looking for value I would bet 1/2 the pot like $14 to keep hands you are ahead of in the pot.  \r\n\r\nShe calls $20 you really need to consider she has you beat.  \r\n\r\nJ on the turn.  Now AJ and JJ have you beat.  TT has picked up an open ended straight draw.  You picked up a single gutter straight draw but your Q might be dead.\r\n\r\nI don't think this lady is going anywhere and you let this be a big pot.  If you keep firing then you are trying to rep AA, AJ, or JJ.  \r\n\r\nAt this point the only hands you are beating that might call are AT, KK, QQ, and TT.  And you don't even want a call from AT or TT.   \r\n\r\nI think it is time to shut is down.  Check the turn and if she fires back then you need to think about folding.  If she checks you could fire the river if you improve or a blank hits.  \r\n\r\nAQo is very playable from middle especially if you are opening. In my opinion you let that pot get too big. 
