17309	2	8911	6ee33d6d-20ac-4fb2-a0d8-d1f772d3f63a	2017-05-03 12:04:42.433	5136	\N	\N	As per Michael, with standard poker it doesn't matter insofar as your ranking, however in some live games what you declare is taken as what your actual hand is so be mindful of this and organise your cards in a fashion whereby you know what you have, and moving deeper into the levelling theory, what your opponents may have in a given situation. \r\n\r\nIn games like badugi, which you may not have explored, the order somewhat matters, as its the lowest card in a suit that plays. \r\n\r\nhttps://www.pagat.com/poker/variants/badugi.html
