17370	5	8929	c8df5f20-d6d6-4cb6-ae27-3a4ff26d51d5	2017-05-09 16:47:35.767	3876	\N	deleted 1 character in body	Provided there is no flush possible, it's a split pot. Both players have the same best 5-card hand of `T J Q K A`.There are no other cards any player can have in Holdem which would improve their hand.\r\n\r\nThere is an existing question on this site about [the top five cards rule and how it applies to splitting pots](https://poker.stackexchange.com/questions/402/what-is-thetop-five-cards-rule-and-how-does-it-apply-to-splitting-pots), as well as one on [how to determine the winning hand in poker](https://poker.stackexchange.com/questions/6680/how-to-determine-the-winning-hands-in-poker), both of which probably answer your question in more detail.
