variation plays out and whether or not my gut feel with regards to strategy is right or not.
17345	2	8924	c05b757d-b180-4e1b-8ba0-c45a1c309737	2017-05-07 01:30:21.047	3876	\N	\N	Not going to have an open ended straight draw on an uncoordinated board.\r\n\r\nThis is just an opinion.  I have not run any simulations.\r\n\r\nIf it only cost 1 BB to see a flop you should be seeing more flops. Even 27o can flop the nuts.   \r\n\r\nPost flop is tricky. You have basically no fold equity. If only 2 see the flop then play Ace plus.  If 3 any pair or better (not counting pair on the board) or 14+ outs. If more than 3 see the flop then any two pair or better (not counting pair on the board) or 14+ outs beating a pair (not counting pair on the board).\r\n\r\nAt 14 outs you are at near 50% go draw out.\r\n
