17915	5	1577	b2e35f79-7ceb-4f67-9031-08d663428b61	2017-07-07 15:36:12.11	674	\N	Corrected math for known board cards.	There are `45 × 44 ÷ 2 = 990` possible starting hands that can be dealt preflop to an opponent when you are heads up, discounting the known cards.  (We divide by two previously because the order that the cards are dealt is irrelevant.) \r\n\r\nIn the situation that you have described above, he can have three of those starting hands, so the odds of a randomly dealt hand being one of those three would be 3 out of 990, which is 1:330, or 0.30% of the time.\r\n\r\nI you have two opponents, the odds for the second opponent would be calculated in a similar manner, and you add the two together to determine the odds of either opponent having the hand.
