17928	2	9112	30ca158b-838b-4bfe-8586-83284e166cdd	2017-07-08 10:20:09.98	5050	\N	\N	First of all, you shouldn't focus on your win rate, but on your decision making. These sit & go's are high very variance, win rate after even 100 sit & go's are not accurate at all. But to answer your question:\n\nThe **heads-up** win rate to be profitable really depends on the rake percentage. Your rate to be nor winning nor losing can be calculated like this:\n\nWin rate = entry fee / (1st place prize * 2)\n\nThe win rate should usually be around 52-56%. If it is higher than this I recommend you to find another format or client.\n\nNow **6-max** is a little more difficult, since 2 spots pay. To make this a bit more easy we should assume that if you get heads-up you will win 50% of the time. Your top 2 win rate can be calculated as follows:\n\nWin rate = entry fee / (1/2 * 1st place + 2nd place)\n\nThis number should be around 35-39%.
