17988	5	6585	b418fdea-2973-4957-a649-8abc795310b7	2017-07-12 14:51:36.983	3876	\N	added 292 characters in body	Pre flop call looking to hit a set is fine. \r\n\r\nOn the flop I would have bet out like 1/2 the pot hoping he has a pair and to fold out the straight draw (KQ J9). If you get raised then you need to consider you may be behind. If you get smooth called then bet out again on the turn and river with 1/2 the pot sized bets. But this is about slow play. \r\n\r\nOn the flop checking you risk it checks around. \r\n\r\nOn the flop check check bet. That could be a made hand or just a cbet. You are hoping he has a pair. If he is on a bigger set that is poker. \r\n\r\nGiven you checked I think slow play is max value here. If the board pairs and they improve to trips you might get it all in. The risk on that board is the straight draw but that probably would have checked. \r\n\r\nIf you raise the risk is you fold out a pair. Even a small raise they call with a pair but then shut down on the turn.  Call is the proper play.\r\n\r\nSlow play when there is little risk of being out drawn and stacks are a good size. Clearly it is easier to slow play in position.\r\n\r\nA down side is that if you always slow play monsters then your bluffs are not successful. \r\n    \r\nLet say that flop was KJ3 you still like your hand but there maybe slow play to get all the chips in and take your chances.  Here if you lead out on the flop and get raised you don't really know where you stand.  You could get raised by a pair of Kings. If they had trip K or J they would slow play you.
17989	5	6585	23310a20-0663-4578-882d-8eb46da770c8	2017-07-12 18:56:14.66	3876	\N	added 364 characters in body	Pre flop call looking to hit a set is fine. \r\n\r\nOn the flop I would have bet out like 1/2 the pot hoping he has a pair and to fold out the straight draw (KQ J9). If you get raised then you need to consider you may be behind. If you get smooth called then bet out again on the turn and river with 1/2 the pot sized bets. But this is about slow play. \r\n\r\nOn the flop checking you risk it checks around. \r\n\r\nOn the flop check check bet. That could be a made hand or just a cbet. You are hoping he has a pair. If he is on a bigger set that is poker. \r\n\r\nGiven you checked I think slow play is max value here. If the board pairs and they improve to trips you might get it all in. The risk on that board is the straight draw but that probably would have checked. \r\n\r\nIf you raise the risk is you fold out a pair. Even a small raise they call with a pair but then shut down on the turn.  Call is the proper play.\r\n\r\nSlow play when there is little risk of being out drawn and stacks are a good size. Clearly it is easier to slow play in position.\r\n\r\nA down side is that if you always slow play monsters then your bluffs are not successful. \r\n\r\nPre flop you should always open monsters JJ+ with a raise as you don't want to let trash hands hit a flop.  From mid to late if someone puts in a small raise then you can sometimes slow play AA KK but you take the chance they hit a set.  There is that famous [hand][1] where slow play AA got bluffed off.\r\n    \r\nLet say that flop was KJ3 you still like your hand but there maybe slow play to get all the chips in and take your chances.  Here if you lead out on the flop and get raised you don't really know where you stand.  You could get raised by a pair of Kings. If they had trip K or J they would slow play you.\r\n\r\n\r\n  [1]: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b2V-EAit-ko
