18043	2	9146	f640f90c-6ca1-44f2-9221-d78d72e69f07	2017-07-15 13:20:02.663	3876	\N	\N	This just a copy of guest geek with more detail  \r\nI tested it out my self\r\n\r\nTurns out this a [BinomialDistribution][1]\r\n\r\n> Binomial distribution is the distribution of a total number of\r\n> successes in a given number of Bernoulli trials. The common notation\r\n> is b(k; n, p), where k is the number of successes, n is the number of\r\n> trials, p is the probability of success.   \r\n> We know that b(k; n, p) = C(n, k) x p^k x (1 - p)^(n - k)\r\n\r\nC(n, k) x p^k x (1 - p)^(n - k)  \r\nC is combination   \r\nx is multiply  \r\n^ if power   \r\np is probability of pocket pair = 1/17  \r\nn is number of hands  \r\nk is number of hands with pocket pair   \r\n\r\n    k                   cumulative\r\n    0 0.5453943226371 0.5453943226371\r\n    1 0.3408714516482 0.8862657742854\r\n    2 0.0958700957761 0.9821358700614\r\n    3 0.0159783492960 0.9981142193574\r\n    4 0.0017476319543 0.9998618513117\r\n    5 0.0001310723966 0.9999929237083\r\n    6 0.0000068266873 0.9999997503956\r\n    7 0.0000002438103 0.9999999942058\r\n    8 0.0000000057143 0.9999999999201\r\n    9 0.0000000000794 0.9999999999995\r\n    10 0.0000000000005 1.0000000000000\r\n\r\nThe cumulative converging to 1 indicates it is correct  \r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.cut-the-knot.org/Curriculum/Probability/BinomialDistribution.shtml
18044	5	9146	84fc43ea-562b-4a2c-a098-b284721da5d3	2017-07-15 13:27:34.487	3876	\N	added 41 characters in body	This just a copy of guest geek with more detail  \r\nI tested it out my self\r\n\r\nTurns out this a [BinomialDistribution][1]\r\n\r\n> Binomial distribution is the distribution of a total number of\r\n> successes in a given number of Bernoulli trials. The common notation\r\n> is b(k; n, p), where k is the number of successes, n is the number of\r\n> trials, p is the probability of success.   \r\n> We know that b(k; n, p) = C(n, k) x p^k x (1 - p)^(n - k)\r\n\r\nC(n, k) x p^k x (1 - p)^(n - k)  \r\nC is combination   \r\nx is multiply  \r\n^ is power   \r\np is probability of pocket pair = 1/17  \r\nn is number of hands  \r\nk is number of hands with pocket pair   \r\n\r\n    k                   cumulative\r\n    0 0.5453943226371 0.5453943226371\r\n    1 0.3408714516482 0.8862657742854\r\n    2 0.0958700957761 0.9821358700614\r\n    3 0.0159783492960 0.9981142193574\r\n    4 0.0017476319543 0.9998618513117\r\n    5 0.0001310723966 0.9999929237083\r\n    6 0.0000068266873 0.9999997503956\r\n    7 0.0000002438103 0.9999999942058\r\n    8 0.0000000057143 0.9999999999201\r\n    9 0.0000000000794 0.9999999999995\r\n    10 0.0000000000005 1.0000000000000\r\n\r\nThe cumulative converging to 1 indicates it is correct  \r\n\r\nI am amazed how quickly it drops off \r\n\r\n  [1]: http://www.cut-the-knot.org/Curriculum/Probability/BinomialDistribution.shtml
