18089	2	9162	3b3ad9a0-5acf-4987-9c23-262551e3fa19	2017-07-19 23:04:33	3876	\N	\N	Well when you go all-in there is no implied odds  \r\n\r\nOn the flop if you go all in then you are not going to face another bet so you can go with the odds of the next two card which is about 36% = 1/2.75  \r\nThe odds of not getting it is  (100 - 36) /  36 = 1.75 : 1  \r\n\r\nYou would be risking 50 to get 80 so you pot odds are 8 : 5 = 1.6 : 1  \r\n\r\nPot odd < hand odds so you should not call  \r\nAnd you could be drawing dead to a bigger flush  \r\n\r\nActually it is 35% but same answer  \r\n\r\n
18090	5	9162	4fd98295-6970-44c8-b34e-cfe8afa1e91c	2017-07-19 23:14:46.873	3876	\N	added 77 characters in body	Well when you go all-in there is no implied odds  \r\n\r\nOn the flop if you go all in then you are not going to face another bet so you can go with the odds of the next two card which is about 36% = 1/2.75  \r\nThe odds of not getting it is  (100 - 36) /  36 = 1.75 : 1  \r\n\r\nYou would be risking 50 to get 80 so you pot odds are 8 : 5 = 1.6 : 1  \r\n\r\nPot odd < hand odds so you should not call  \r\nAnd you could be drawing dead to a bigger flush  \r\n\r\nActually it is 35% but same answer.  36% includes if 2 flush come up and then you can lose to a single flush.    \r\n\r\n
