18143	2	9173	4e3a603e-026f-4582-b8da-c45a51838bd7	2017-07-28 17:42:01.383	3876	\N	\N	I suggest you write an equity calculator first as a bot needs one. If you base stuff off equity it is so much easier. Then just a binary made or draw hand.\r\n\r\nThen you can just do an odds for call and give a fixed implied odds on a draw. If you need 3:1 to call on a draw go with one less 2:1. All you have left is bet sizing for open and re-raise. Bluffs is a little harder but if you just bluff your busted draws like 1/3 you will be pretty close.  \r\n\r\nCall bluffs is a little harder but you are going to get some stats on how often they call when you just call for equity.  Call back about 1/3 to 1/2 of their bluff rate if you have a bluff catcher.  \r\n\r\nAssign an open range for each position and bet sizing.  Flop sizing like 1/5 is enough to throw them off.  \r\n\r\nI tried a GTO based bot but it was a disaster. GTO you are playing not to lose.\r\n\r\nBased on play you can just range of the opponents.  If you base logic on equity then you don't need complex rules.
