18348	2	9243	e3862b92-6031-4706-a7e3-1a37289e8125	2017-08-21 21:29:17.96	\N	user4555	\N	I used to play a game called **Seven Card Sweat**.\r\n\r\nThe game was very simple and it was purely for fun / to gamble. It is also very similar to what you are describing.\r\n\r\nEach player is dealt seven cards face-down. The first player reveals their first card and stops. The second player reveals cards until they have a hand that beats the other players. This continues until all players have revealed all of their cards, and the player with the best hand at the end wins all of the money. \r\n\r\nFor example two players:\r\n\r\n*Each get dealt seven cards face-down.*\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; --- `King High`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; --- `Ace High`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; --- `Pair of Fours`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; A&diamond; --- `Pair of Aces`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; K&clubs; --- `Two Pair; Kings and Fours`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; A&diamond; 4&clubs; 7&spades; 5&spades; --- `Straight; Ace through Five`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; K&clubs; K&hearts; --- `Full House; Kings full of Fours`\r\n\r\n<br>\r\nPlayer B: *"Wow that's so sick. Take your money!"*\r\n \r\nIt can be played with as many players as the deck allows, which is seven.
18349	5	9243	6fd934da-302d-4233-8f4f-588c9fdb7600	2017-08-21 21:34:46.12	\N	user4555	Refined rules.	I used to play a game called **Seven Card Sweat**.\r\n\r\nThe game was very simple and it was purely for fun / to gamble. It is also very similar to what you are describing.\r\n\r\nEach player is dealt seven cards face-down. The first player reveals their first card and stops. The second player reveals cards until they have a five-or-less card hand that beats the other players. This continues until all players have revealed all of their cards, and the player with the best five card hand at the end wins all of the money. \r\n\r\nThe turn taking is purely for entertainment e.g. the *sweat* aspect. There is no strategy.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFor example two players:\r\n\r\n*Each get dealt seven cards face-down.*\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; --- `King High`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; --- `Ace High`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; --- `Pair of Fours`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; A&diamond; --- `Pair of Aces`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; K&clubs; --- `Two Pair; Kings and Fours`\r\n\r\nPlayer B: 2&diamond; 3&hearts; A&spades; A&diamond; 4&clubs; 7&spades; 5&spades; --- `Straight; Ace through Five`\r\n\r\nPlayer A: K&spades; 8&diamond; 4&hearts; 9&clubs; 4&diamond; K&clubs; K&hearts; --- `Full House; Kings full of Fours`\r\n\r\n<br>\r\nPlayer B: *"Wow that's so sick. Take your money!"*\r\n \r\nIt can be played with as many players as the deck allows, which is seven.
