18423	2	9264	9bbf0ff6-25a9-4cfb-9062-86b25d6d05bb	2017-08-27 20:58:43.427	5419	\N	\N	It all depends on how deeply you want to investigate the game. If you wish to understand odds and strategies at the deepest level, you'll be looking at game theory. If you do want to go that deeply you'll first have to learn about Linear algebra, single/multi variable calculus, methods of proof in mathematics, possibly some real analysis and definitely differential equations. \r\n\r\nYou'll then progress to game theory where you'll learn about imperfect information games which is a field of current research as well, so from there you'll go as deeply in to the theory of poker as is currently known.\r\n\r\nIf you don't want to go too deeply, some simple arithmetic and some probability theory is enough to set you up very well.
