18479	2	9287	bab06dc7-3da7-4f9f-a7e4-35030f6ae652	2017-09-01 19:14:55.89	3876	\N	\N	**Pre**   \r\nI am going to assume AA, KK, QQ, AKs would raise.  Maybe JJ TT.  \r\n\r\n**Flop**  \r\nCalled a bet of 3/4 the flop.  He can have a set, an over pair, or a flush draw.  You block some of the flush draws. AJs, ATs, AKo with a diamond maybe KJs, JTs.  I don't see him connecting with the straight.\r\n\r\n**Turn**   \r\nYou pick up a flush draw in case he is on a set.  You have to call here so you might as well bet.  A pot sized bet from villain just tells you he can still have a set, an over pair, a flush, or AKo with a diamond.  I think the nut flush would have checked back. \r\n\r\n**River**  \r\nYou are getting 2:1. Same thing set, an over pair, a flush, or AKo with a diamond. I am not seeing many bluffs that get here. Unless he was also bluffing the turn. You should have bet the turn. KK and AKs would have raised pre.  AKo could call that flop and bet the turn when you showed weakness.  He is not putting you on a flush or set since you checked the turn. You called the turn so he is most likely putting you on an over pair. So he is not value betting 99 TT.  His only value bet is JJ, set, a flush, and a pair of kings. Is he putting an advance double barrel bluff on you? AQ, AJ, and AT with a single diamond could get here.\r\n\r\nHe can do this with J(4), 77(3), 22(3), 6(3), 88(3), AKo with a diamond(12), and 4 diamond draws.  \r\n28:4 < 2:1     \r\nI don't agree you can call his value range.\r\n\r\nYou need to think he can make some single diamond hands that get here into a bluff to call. But I don't think so. I don't even think there is enough bluffs to call 2:1.\r\n  
