18644	2	9348	26d6d2e0-c839-4ff2-8b80-f3a6edd67ec5	2017-09-27 13:40:07.62	3876	\N	\N	You can only win or lose what is in front of you. If you get AA you want enough in front of you to build a big pot if not get it all in. You still don't want to risk your entire bankroll on a singe hand. Or you make the nuts. 100 BB is a good starting point.  \r\n\r\nIf you feel like you are getting pushed around and want to play smaller pots then you can load up for less.  The minimum is typically 40-60 BB. \r\n\r\nIf you feel you are a good post flop player then you want a big stack.\r\n\r\nOther answer has good numbers for bankroll management.
