18958	2	9448	cf09f541-7a8c-4ed1-84ec-777f7bc3b555	2017-11-06 02:19:39.743	5588	\N	\N	there is one thing i still dont really understand about odds.\r\n\r\nSo imagine we have a open ended flush draw after the flop and villain holds top pair. The pot is 100 after villain bets 40 so we got 2.5:1 odds to call\r\nOur odds to make the flush on the river are 1,86 zu 1.\r\nHowever our odds to make the flush on the turn are only about 4:1.\r\n\r\nShould we still call? What, if we dont hit on the turn do we have to fold it?\r\n \r\nSecond question how much could we call after the flop if we hold top pair + an open ended flush draw while other player holds only two unpaired cards.\r\n\r\nhope you can help me\r\n
