19097	2	9503	70015412-dd37-414c-ab5e-3d93824e6bfb	2017-11-23 15:42:01.317	5050	\N	\N	Like you said, his strategy is bad and this means we can take advantage of this. Since he is a bad player, we will not have to worry about being exploited too much. I'd advice the following approach:\n\n1. Do not play too loose pre-flop. You said he is always calling pre-flop, so taking down the blinds will rarely happen.\n\n2. Raise to a reasonable amount pre-flop. You will have a stronger range than him. Therefore, you want to play a larger pot.\n\n3. He is very passive. I think that with draws and middling hands you should be too. Just check it down until the river. You don't have to win every pot.\n\n4. Wait until you hit a good hand and then bet big.\n\n5. You should bluff sometimes, but the majority of your bets should be for value.
