19717	2	9711	7542793a-b514-4b0a-89e7-994b242a6309	2018-03-06 10:19:00.61	5585	\N	\N	I've been playing poker (all kind of it) for many years. something that happens a lot in home games, is a misdeal. when dealer who happens to be a player, somehow accidentally shows a card when dealing it to players. I supposed that misdeal rules depends on specific house rules, but is there any rule for misdeal in casinos ? \r\n\r\nfor more clarification, I have seen these scenarios:\r\n\r\n - in Texas hold'em, if the shown card was any players first hole card, they interrupt the hand, and the dealing and shuffle and deal from start.\r\n - sometimes, they end the hand if the shown card is first card of first 4 players .\r\n - in many games, they wont end the hand. they consider this shown card first burn (burn before flop), they resume the dealing, instead of shown card, they deal a actual first burn card to the player's shown card.\r\n\r\nmy questions are:\r\n\r\n1. what is the exact definition of misdeal ?\r\n2. what they woulddo in casino regarding misdeal ?\r\n
