19978	2	9805	321ba3a6-804b-4c70-9be0-1b9a03d5f598	2018-04-10 15:27:56.893	3876	\N	\N	Naturally I will not accept my own answer.  My answer is not what the pro advised.  I will post that in the question later.\r\n\r\nThe flop is not very coordinated.  Villain could have 9T, J8, Jx, 8x, or 22.  Seems like JJ or 99 would have raised pre.  Maybe villain is on like 89 and wants to see where he is. Or is on a big J betting for value. \r\n\r\nA raise by the hero is just going to fold out the single pair hands he has beat.  And get called by 2 pr plus hands.  9T would likely checked here.  JJ or 88 would likely have checked that flop.\r\n\r\nType of hand I would just call hoping villain keeps betting.  Best case if villain is on top pair and thinks it is good.  Would even check back the flop hoping villain would bet the river.  I think I would value bet / raise on the river of like 1/2 the pot.
