20089	5	8643	5f477f7b-c51d-4121-bd1a-c7dbee2b3115	2018-04-20 12:11:23.463	3876	\N	added 511 characters in body	"Stayed in the hand at all" is referring to pre-flop call.\r\n\r\nA5 is not that bad of a call pre-flop if it is suited. Calling 4 bb is not so good. If it was 2.5 bb it is a better call. Kind of why AK was mad as they thought 4 bb was enough to chase off A5 and A6.\r\n\r\n - will flop 2 pair or better about 6.88% of the time\r\n - will flop 2 pair or better or 8+ outs to straight or flush or better\r\n   about 18% of the time\r\n\r\nEven a single pair flop if all cards are under 10 is playable.\r\n\r\nAK should not get all that excited. It is still only top pair. Raise 1/2 - 1  pot but I don't see going all in. Behind A6, A5, 56, 55, and 66. I think there are 54 combinations. All of those hands *could* call pre-flop. An overbet is only going to get called by a better hand. Might get called by AQ or AJ.\r\n\r\nIt is not a good pre-flop call but it is not a terrible call.  It stacked the hero.\r\n\r\nSlightly off calls that have ways to win often have good implied odds. Need decent sized stacks to have implied odds. Suited it could make the nut flush. It can make a straight.  
20120	5	9845	2be8c351-b689-4fec-a31f-0f824f3eecfb	2018-04-24 15:47:41.903	4459	\N	added 3 characters in body	When **not** holding a pocket pair:\r\n\r\n    ((4 choose 2) * 11 + (3 choose 2) * 2) / (50 choose 2) = 5.87755%\r\n\r\nWhen holding a pocket pair\r\n\r\n    ((4 choose 2) * 12 + (2 choose 2) * 1) / (50 choose 2) = 5.95918%\r\n\r\nSo your opponent has a slightly _better_  chance of getting a pocket pair when you hold one yourself, but the difference is indeed slight!
