20543	2	9979	4f73b85e-2450-4419-82a7-31f6e2bc4d61	2018-07-12 16:47:37.3	3876	\N	\N	AQs is not a premium hand but you are getting 3:1 on a call and closing out action. The short stacks have a big range. The big stack just flatting is odd. Either they have a monster and want a call or are just taking a chance with a speculative hand on busting out two players. I would just call in that spot hoping to improve on the flop. If you don't improve on the flop and V1 bets you can just fold. 20K is a big investment but you have a chance to knock out 2 and more than triple up.  By just raising pre you give the big stack a chance to push and put you in a tough spot.  If you shove pre you still are still facing two all in and a only a better hand will call.  This is a call for me.
