142	1	\N	\N	2012-01-11 16:25:11.663	\N	30	2615	<p>I've been playing for years at small cash games and in casinos, but not online.  Yet I'm seeing a fair amount of terminology and abbreviations I haven't seen before.  While "Hero" and "Villain" are fairly obvious in meaning, they're not terms I associate with poker terminology.  </p>\n\n<p>There are other terms I've seen used here that might be familiar to some poker players, but not others.</p>\n\n<p>Is there a comprehensive source for commonly used poker terms and abbreviations (and not just the multitude of fun hand names, like "American airlines", "little slick", etc.)?  </p>\n\n<p>If there isn't a good comprehensive source, I'm open to converting this to Community Wiki and compiling our own source.</p>\n	12	\N	\N	\N	\N	2017-07-11 16:37:01.833	Is there a comprehensive source for poker terminology?	<terminology>	8	3	13	\N	\N
