1595	1	1601	\N	2013-10-25 17:57:26.307	\N	7	1092	<p>If you wanted to improve your poker game, what statistics should you track? Do players that keep a track of how much they have won/lost and where do better than players who don't?</p>\n\n<p>I play online (for now) and I'm currently tracking the Date, Day of week, Start Time, End Time, Site, Game Type, Buy In, End Game Balance, Total Profit, Profit Per Hour, Hand Count and Hands per Hour in a spreadsheet. Is this data actually useful? Should I be collecting more data or less?</p>\n	1138	\N	\N	\N	\N	2013-10-27 22:29:17.867	What data should you keep track of to improve your game?	<poker-theory><software><learning>	1	0	3	\N	\N
