2752	1	2761	\N	2014-02-17 17:47:12.037	\N	8	6953	<p>When I get busted it is because I did not identify that my opponent held a set and I thought my top pair with top kicker is best.</p>\n\n<p>I often run in situations where I held something like A&spades;K&spades; and flop looks like 4&hearts;A&diamond;7&clubs;.</p>\n\n<p>It happens often that I see preflop someone limping and than still calling my 5-7xBB.</p>\n\n<p>Now it happens that someone with 4&diamond;4&clubs; plays slow or aggressive or whatever, but I never give them 77 or 44, nor 47 or AA - just because of their preflop betting. And I bet, he raises or goes allin and in most cases it ends in an Allin on the flop.</p>\n\n<p><strong>What is a good strategy to identify such set of fours?</strong></p>\n\n<p>Or is it impossible? Because there are so many bad players out there, that play such cards like they do and on long term they will loose but in this case they get me?</p>\n\n<p>I know, I have to look at stack sizes and how the guy played his last hands and everything. But I did not figure out a good way against such donk-moves.</p>\n	1303	\N	\N	\N	\N	2014-02-22 02:10:35.183	How to identify low sets against top pair top kicker? (Online Poker)	<texas-hold-em><online><betting-strategy><no-limit><poker-strategy>	4	1	\N	\N	\N
