2866	2	\N	2865	2014-04-07 18:03:38.397	\N	5	\N	<p>No, they don't take a cut of anything you cash in or out. They make their money from something called <em>rake</em>.</p>\n\n<p>In a cash game they'll usually take 2-5% if I recall correctly, up to X amount of dollars (it caps at some point). In tournaments a portion of your buy-in will be rake. For instance, consider the $1.10 micro-stakes big field multi-table tournaments on Pokerstars. $1 goes towards the tournament prize pool, $0.10, the rake, goes to PokerStars.</p>\n\n<p>Note that they aren't alone in this regard. Live, brick and mortar casinos do this as well. </p>\n	1431	\N	\N	\N	\N	2014-04-07 18:03:38.397	\N	\N	\N	0	\N	\N	\N
