4248	5	\N	\N	2014-10-01 22:31:51.287	\N	0	\N	<p>Also called the "Dealer Button".</p>\n\n<p>Many forms of poker such as Draw poker and Hold'em poker (Texas Hold'em and Omaha) involve a rotating deal. The deck is passed clockwise each hand to a player. The player then is the dealer for that hand. The dealer has position over all other players, except for the pre-flop street. It's usually symbolized by a big chip with a "D" on it.</p>\n\n<p>The button has no use in Stud games, since other rules are applied in those games to determine who acts next.</p>\n	-1	\N	309	\N	2014-10-02 07:03:11.05	2014-10-02 07:03:11.05	\N	\N	\N	0	\N	\N	\N
