5857	1	\N	\N	2015-04-24 04:41:50.247	\N	2	320	<p>Scenario: I am chip leader and say "All In". The only other player left in the game calls, even though he only has half the chips I do. All my chips are pushed in. I never measure my chip count against his. I just said "All In" and put my chips in. The only other player puts his in to call (even though he has less). He wins the hand easily. Do I lose all my chips now? Or do I just lose as many chips as he had?</p>\n	3261	\N	\N	\N	\N	2015-04-24 04:58:58.803	All in when you are chip leader	<all-in>	1	0	\N	\N	\N
