8571	2	\N	8568	2017-01-01 01:40:18.23	\N	0	\N	<p>In your specific example, someone holding the 7&spades; beats anyone not holding a spade in their hand.</p>\n\n<p>Anyone holding 7&spades; or higher (and therefore can beat the board) beats anyone who doesn't (and is therefore playing the board).</p>\n\n<p>Anyone with 7&spades;8&spades; has the nuts with a straight flush and cannot be beaten. Next is 7&spades;3&spades; and then 3&spades;2&spades; for smaller straight flushes.</p>\n\n<p>If no one has a straight flush and multiple players have a spade which is 7 or higher, the highest spade wins.</p>\n\n<p>If no-one has a spade 7 or higher, it's a split pot.</p>\n	4771	\N	4771	\N	2017-01-01 01:45:23.46	2017-01-01 01:45:23.46	\N	\N	\N	5	\N	\N	\N
