9216	2	\N	2863	2017-08-10 17:14:13.653	\N	0	\N	<p>When you get two calls behind you and a raise you are behind.  But you are getting 3.6:1 so call.  </p>\n\n<p>On the flop you have top pair on a dry board.  Not sure why you are looking to fold out worse hands. If you have the best hand it is likely to hold up. </p>\n\n<p>You are ahead or behind and that is not likely to change.  I know it did but villain spiked a two outer.</p>\n\n<p>I don't put villain on KQ or KJ as that was a good raise pre. I would put him on JJ+ or AKs.</p>\n\n<p>Betting 1/2 the pot kind of lets you know where you stand but I would prefer check call unless they bet the pot or more.</p>\n\n<p>Even if you bet the pot QQ might have called but you need to consider that you are behind AK, AA, KK.</p>\n\n<p>Great turn for you.  You are only behind KK and QQ which is certainly in villains range but even if they are tight then less then 1/2 the range.</p>\n\n<p>You might as well put them all in.  </p>\n\n<p>When you get re-raised you are probably behind but with the pot odds you need to call.  </p>\n	3876	\N	\N	\N	\N	2017-08-10 17:14:13.653	\N	\N	\N	0	\N	\N	\N
