9617	2	\N	9616	2018-01-28 00:22:14.717	\N	8	\N	<p>Google  </p>\n\n<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overlay_(poker)" rel="noreferrer">Wiki</a></p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>In poker, an overlay is the gap between a poker tournament's\n  guaranteed prize pool and the actual prize pool generated by entrants.</p>\n  \n  <p>For example, if a tournament has a guaranteed prize pool of $10,000, a\n  buy in of $100 and 90 players enter, the players will contribute only\n  $9,000 to the prizepool. The rest of the prizepool (in this example\n  $1,000)—made up by the tournament host—would be the overlay for the\n  tournament.</p>\n</blockquote>\n	3876	\N	\N	\N	\N	2018-01-28 00:22:14.717	\N	\N	\N	0	\N	\N	\N
