1084	913	2013-09-18 18:52:51.613	Paulpro	2018-08-01 17:32:56.927	\N	Canada	<p>For years Bitcoin adoption has been slower than expected, because Bitcoin has been becoming unnecessarily complex in the guise of avoiding hard forks. On August 1, 2017 that changed when Bitcoin hardforked to implement the first substantial network upgrade in many years. The hardfork was contentious, causing a split where both the non-forked and forked version of the coin continue to exist. The legacy version has financial backing by big banks that want to slow bitcoin adoption and has kept the name Bitcoin.</p>\n\n<p>The upgraded version is now called Bitcoin Cash and will hardfork (non-contentiously) on a regular interval every six months, allowing the network to be upgraded without catching any node operators off guard. In the first hardfork Bitcoin Cash removed RBF so that merchants can now accept unconfirmed transactions, and increased the block size so that it can scale to support more transactions and have lower fees. The next upgrade will fix TX malleability in a much simpler way than segwit does (segwit is needlessly complex in order to avoid a hardfork) and fix it for all transactions instead of only fixing it only for segwit transactions. Many more exciting upgrades will be rolled out in the biannual hardforks.</p>\n\n<p>Supporting Bitcoin Cash over Bitcoin is a vote for the ability to upgrade the network and removing the influence of big banks.</p>\n	12	107	32	https://i.stack.imgur.com/UjMVq.jpg?s=128&g=1	\N	\N	403973
